c24444af2795ba87a624129b21cdb5ac00132dbcf5c1e8ec6a6a13a/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-103178/ma-source-field/0fb16e5afc24444af2795ba87a624129b21cdb5ac00132dbcf5c1e8ec6a6a13a/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-103178/ma-source-field/0fb16e5afc24444af2795ba87a624129b21cdb5ac00132dbcf5c1e8ec6a6a13a/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-103178/ma-source-field/0fb16e5afc24444af2795ba87a624129b21cdb5ac00132dbcf5c1e8ec6a6a13a/343e05bc561f1754cb89989f943a6f3c9344f2abea94d650b67c7b53d017c0c6"] :answer-field/correct "q-103178/ma-source-field/0fb16e5afc24444af2795ba87a624129b21cdb5ac00132dbcf5c1e8ec6a6a13a/343e05bc561f1754cb89989f943a6f3c9344f2abea94d650b67c7b53d017c0c6" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103178" :question/id #uuid "8e4d2f85-2640-5963-a9fc-d023ea35768b" :question/math-academy-id "q-103178" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $P(x,y)?$\n\nI. $y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y$\nII. $xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$\nIII. $y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-1\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{x}^{2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$  gives an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is ''III only''." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103178/ma-source-field/0fb16e5afc24444af2795ba87a624129b21cdb5ac00132dbcf5c1e8ec6a6a13a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103178"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858/168842c5b03a67891d93d79c4ab96e78a0ee7339ba24ef18175211d342d74752" :answer/id #uuid "da75cf17-b00a-5ed0-97c9-6265dae86079" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-1$ and $x=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858/8dd0139fe2bdff82a7de02af21e81b3fb0031e695d60709e4cec3b9cfa395bee" :answer/id #uuid "d02a6f82-debb-558b-a876-dc02aab50551" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-1$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858/52a2923487b050232d479cf31908a2c6486c62f308c06a60c224f2e87126c6e9" :answer/id #uuid "8c127ea3-d160-5664-896d-8df951530b12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-2$ and $x=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858/1f5e9570249f9e2622f3d5d63abffa3331e89a167568104f9602084907c01516" :answer/id #uuid "77df7b4b-c87e-5e29-808b-f38574caacd1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=1$ and $x=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" :answer/id #uuid "54ba84a1-3d25-5cd1-98bf-f731c2622e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858" :answer-field/id #uuid "53daf543-087e-50bb-928d-d5b44cae5b1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858/168842c5b03a67891d93d79c4ab96e78a0ee7339ba24ef18175211d342d74752" "q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858/8dd0139fe2bdff82a7de02af21e81b3fb0031e695d60709e4cec3b9cfa395bee" "q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858/52a2923487b050232d479cf31908a2c6486c62f308c06a60c224f2e87126c6e9" "q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858/1f5e9570249f9e2622f3d5d63abffa3331e89a167568104f9602084907c01516" "q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042"] :answer-field/correct "q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858/168842c5b03a67891d93d79c4ab96e78a0ee7339ba24ef18175211d342d74752" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104025" :question/id #uuid "c6685bf3-2db8-58de-88bd-a80799c06e2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-104025" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2d342689f9e4a213ac5407ccc132868b51ba218afabda1a871e7ca7b02345a17.png)\n\nWhat are the points of discontinuity of the function plotted above?" :question/worked-solution "The graph breaks at $x=-1$ and $x=2,$ meaning that we can't draw the plot without taking our pencil off of the paper when passing through these points.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-1$ and $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104025/ma-source-field/3e1a665512e12c19abba0006e852b68d128869b4fe78f64b55bce502faa6c858"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31eacf5a-75a5-5b38-8c24-4b1598ecf3a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104025"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7/042526f0f149ecdc71a38ff369b428df94fe7b45e30f66bc4fcc4a3e4c26d45f" :answer/id #uuid "e5f3b240-c702-580d-9cdf-43123253f773" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7/e8057b6831062ce6ab13a510c53035204819425697a814aafca5df2df68ebcc4" :answer/id #uuid "3bf8a5fb-65f3-58d7-a288-3f0a87f9681a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7/6a145e4334efe339650b8b70a32aec06578133b46b600eab008353c52a2a70e3" :answer/id #uuid "640a91d9-57f7-5e99-bc15-29e1456e8af0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7/c0bb241511534a82ed83bf9f68ac61e0b32368db71a28bd7cf3b67bde4af7283" :answer/id #uuid "2044901c-e971-534a-af35-fba5ec803324" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7/51a095e0b68bf5e4f23f4ce05cd97d0463c784481999fd29715f89caae21911b" :answer/id #uuid "574dea89-ee9d-5556-a72b-c257c732699e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "a01010bc-5e11-583a-98fc-7b20994c0fc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7/042526f0f149ecdc71a38ff369b428df94fe7b45e30f66bc4fcc4a3e4c26d45f" "q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7/e8057b6831062ce6ab13a510c53035204819425697a814aafca5df2df68ebcc4" "q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7/6a145e4334efe339650b8b70a32aec06578133b46b600eab008353c52a2a70e3" "q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7/c0bb241511534a82ed83bf9f68ac61e0b32368db71a28bd7cf3b67bde4af7283" "q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7/51a095e0b68bf5e4f23f4ce05cd97d0463c784481999fd29715f89caae21911b"] :answer-field/correct "q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7/c0bb241511534a82ed83bf9f68ac61e0b32368db71a28bd7cf3b67bde4af7283" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105291" :question/id #uuid "faa7ddb4-5b88-5e56-a53e-35fdb9d2ef93" :question/math-academy-id "q-105291" :question/problem "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105291/ma-source-field/71c53a7634912cb6f031344fbe75bcdbc5c96062c1de8b7149ec25d630c495c7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5130f54d-2a53-5373-81a6-355921ea7523"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105291"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56/e1fc478b411592e58e576448691053e9633d1468a76b5b3bd4bf64be4b8fde16" :answer/id #uuid "257d280c-e23a-51f0-8ab9-6c6a6d270300" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\cdot p\\ne p$ for some $p\\in Y$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56/0bcdbb5e1d8578fbb302f902f9215efe0f182b4e5bbfcd202fcd22e782901d36" :answer/id #uuid "cb6dcbd0-7e6a-5124-8dfb-30e54362007c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56/41486ea51f484622f0661e7a8b55a516fd68f7adbeb4f14f3692ec3fc17350d8" :answer/id #uuid "3afd6545-9a30-5d6b-bce2-014c2d72383f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56/0254c053a8fcf9e56483b2456fce38aaf17ebd8281a4ef72b0e22e947931a0b7" :answer/id #uuid "0a58b77f-aa33-52d3-a1ab-4bbbe9ed2639" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not associative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56/4323da32f4d0e343524480efb3fc2e33f66f54e3b33c2db4aac6648792846d8c" :answer/id #uuid "8ab25e26-7932-539a-b22c-b438766b2222" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not commutative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e07246a-b3d7-5b8e-9074-824239bfbe46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56/e1fc478b411592e58e576448691053e9633d1468a76b5b3bd4bf64be4b8fde16" "q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56/0bcdbb5e1d8578fbb302f902f9215efe0f182b4e5bbfcd202fcd22e782901d36" "q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56/41486ea51f484622f0661e7a8b55a516fd68f7adbeb4f14f3692ec3fc17350d8" "q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56/0254c053a8fcf9e56483b2456fce38aaf17ebd8281a4ef72b0e22e947931a0b7" "q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56/4323da32f4d0e343524480efb3fc2e33f66f54e3b33c2db4aac6648792846d8c"] :answer-field/correct "q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56/41486ea51f484622f0661e7a8b55a516fd68f7adbeb4f14f3692ec3fc17350d8" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106929" :question/id #uuid "4c206776-99db-55ba-ae48-7c0ec7d6d597" :question/math-academy-id "q-106929" :question/problem "Let $Y$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x\\in R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree exactly $2.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed.** *\n\nIndeed, let's consider, for example, the polynomials $p(x)={x}^{2}+x$ and $q(x)=-{x}^{2}.$ Then $p,q\\in Y,$ but \n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)={x}^{2}+x+(-{x}^{2})=x\\notin Y\n$$\n\n because $\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p+q)=1\\ne 2.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- $1\\cdot p=p$ for all $p\\in Y.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106929/ma-source-field/8705092b1ffa7a691e12905f2d7383556e4bb281ade18fefc3015cd573606e56"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106929"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801/39ce4feac3754f14f312ebbf40b6b6942599ab62d9f7528045b3064023739dd6" :answer/id #uuid "b0fcd6c1-3e34-5869-bda3-f3935c249cfe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in L$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801/eb57353034a62a867325ffbf5c3603e09d85e72840a34606df91d959ee49bb75" :answer/id #uuid "85442eb9-7db8-592f-9879-ddfd77d97231" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions in $L$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801/af0eba804fe4e1984fdee36b872595a6820b8598cca0173b2959526c5870f5f7" :answer/id #uuid "dac8d022-edf8-56b5-99c7-7f2b00e051d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of functions in $L$ is not associative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801/c26bc0b99b0b461cbb162012172b782569b27c43d4a833b5412a2affe482fe80" :answer/id #uuid "6358779e-1da8-5238-9ef6-81ac25fc065f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of functions in $L$ is not commutative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801/83f490698e6e183c9c2b74efe3d16ee9060e1e0d6cfa7bd24f10d24f6c178e00" :answer/id #uuid "9ae69b77-733b-5c58-bc2b-3800bcfe26dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801" :answer-field/id #uuid "f09dfa2c-f035-539f-94db-4698ecc43f0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801/39ce4feac3754f14f312ebbf40b6b6942599ab62d9f7528045b3064023739dd6" "q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801/eb57353034a62a867325ffbf5c3603e09d85e72840a34606df91d959ee49bb75" "q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801/af0eba804fe4e1984fdee36b872595a6820b8598cca0173b2959526c5870f5f7" "q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801/c26bc0b99b0b461cbb162012172b782569b27c43d4a833b5412a2affe482fe80" "q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801/83f490698e6e183c9c2b74efe3d16ee9060e1e0d6cfa7bd24f10d24f6c178e00"] :answer-field/correct "q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801/83f490698e6e183c9c2b74efe3d16ee9060e1e0d6cfa7bd24f10d24f6c178e00" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930" :question/id #uuid "15beea94-47dc-575a-be81-e2d3b2547e2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-106930" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form $f(x)=ax+1,$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$L$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$L$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =2$ and $f(x)=x+1,$ then $\\alpha f(x)=2x+2.$ So, $\\alpha f(x)\\notin L$ because the constant term is not $1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in L.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of real valued functions satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106930/ma-source-field/63683f59ef36b06ee829c06b20181766c556038dae9a19fc64d4794864f4e801"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106930"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e/cf84a0be6615cf8b724267d39f017290147872766eceddaea4686d5e27a46450" :answer/id #uuid "d6932b0d-e307-5cc8-971a-38fac820cb2a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in I$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e/e55795f52c0d0e93eff79a551178375b18905c082b9082558435009d8e152041" :answer/id #uuid "4d629cc1-8c34-5761-b952-696843bcc069" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$I$ does not contain the zero element" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e/b995fa6cee691762cad1e47239d32ebacbe46cf3a5779155ece45a65cb734a18" :answer/id #uuid "1e058a54-9658-5798-ba7c-a86d9840498e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e/a29949613cd73e7af1d3c653ec985c36c4b83d47dd8e99a1667450b4724c40f4" :answer/id #uuid "7cd140b2-7871-5579-9e98-6ecf9f3f51ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of functions is not associative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e/9c279caa6b673c706cd42011414b98049ca7811e50b185c29ff9238347b5513a" :answer/id #uuid "62b7fc67-e9bb-5a0f-8e80-9dcf56649314" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of functions is not commutative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7ef701a-1be0-572c-baca-f76e42023271" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e/cf84a0be6615cf8b724267d39f017290147872766eceddaea4686d5e27a46450" "q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e/e55795f52c0d0e93eff79a551178375b18905c082b9082558435009d8e152041" "q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e/b995fa6cee691762cad1e47239d32ebacbe46cf3a5779155ece45a65cb734a18" "q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e/a29949613cd73e7af1d3c653ec985c36c4b83d47dd8e99a1667450b4724c40f4" "q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e/9c279caa6b673c706cd42011414b98049ca7811e50b185c29ff9238347b5513a"] :answer-field/correct "q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e/e55795f52c0d0e93eff79a551178375b18905c082b9082558435009d8e152041" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106933" :question/id #uuid "17d56701-363e-5629-ba43-f0ff54124002" :question/math-academy-id "q-106933" :question/problem "Let $I$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form $f(x)={2}^{ax},$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$I$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, $f(x)={2}^{ax}>0$ for all $x\\in R$ for any $a\\in R,$ hence the zero function $z(x)=0\\notin I.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in I.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is commutative. $\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106933/ma-source-field/841c6c3432c6b46f5764a363e7054fc01bbbe051af8f425f64cf24ad22fbb77e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106933"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109247/ma-source-field/314b7086d8e45bd4a380840791ef759223168d49ae5b593928fe857bc1aa873e/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "776b96b0-8f5c-5b47-aa83-d1f82dd2dcf5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109247/ma-source-field/314b7086d8e45bd4a380840791ef759223168d49ae5b593928fe857bc1aa873e/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "c4860770-5064-5335-8f48-a983fc3e37dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109247/ma-source-field/314b7086d8e45bd4a380840791ef759223168d49ae5b593928fe857bc1aa873e/f073cec77042b855fcc95ae59e5c07a0d566930857e27de8effde7dcda1f144f" :answer/id #uuid "1eab1cd1-046e-5de3-9cd8-3170cc92f482" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109247/ma-source-field/314b70