e block lower triangular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $B$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109247/ma-source-field/314b7086d8e45bd4a380840791ef759223168d49ae5b593928fe857bc1aa873e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109247"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733/8548bd60179d299eff7d6747f28965504d3f34e77b39a1393c83c8f18ac5f2ff" :answer/id #uuid "68909286-13b5-56f8-91c1-b39ee0c858f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)={e}^{2x}$ and $b=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733/42425508260aaac0bb9b75c117f5aa70006afc090bdfbbaf7626176060efe58c" :answer/id #uuid "d9ab5d51-4c5d-5e5c-bd82-b3125ac54774" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)={e}^{6x}$ and $b=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733/18c8c2e802b239aec5e0068b977dd2e986ca2cb9cfb472d5337b8d531de74d73" :answer/id #uuid "34cc89b8-44ed-5197-913c-4b08fc997159" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)={e}^{6x}$ and $b=6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733/cd2f4f1ba4b85266177b8d2de99c4fd5e2a46a1fa3e4a1887198aa78a4362d72" :answer/id #uuid "e106c9d7-5e46-53e8-bd3f-34d8e8d97090" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $b=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733/284e335524189faa6f766ad48fcb3df16b33ea88eeb30a8546fc0d07ba5a1687" :answer/id #uuid "e2308dd8-f04b-55a3-a357-4d4562b92a56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $b=6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733" :answer-field/id #uuid "224da74b-2945-552e-a5c2-10b9f76d854e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733/8548bd60179d299eff7d6747f28965504d3f34e77b39a1393c83c8f18ac5f2ff" "q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733/42425508260aaac0bb9b75c117f5aa70006afc090bdfbbaf7626176060efe58c" "q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733/18c8c2e802b239aec5e0068b977dd2e986ca2cb9cfb472d5337b8d531de74d73" "q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733/cd2f4f1ba4b85266177b8d2de99c4fd5e2a46a1fa3e4a1887198aa78a4362d72" "q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733/284e335524189faa6f766ad48fcb3df16b33ea88eeb30a8546fc0d07ba5a1687"] :answer-field/correct "q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733/284e335524189faa6f766ad48fcb3df16b33ea88eeb30a8546fc0d07ba5a1687" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113918" :question/id #uuid "c2081a2b-f662-517d-bd66-e0ddf60008b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-113918" :question/problem "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{6i/n}\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}].$" :question/worked-solution "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=0.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{6}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{n}=\\frac{b-0}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=6.\n$$\n\nConsequently,  ${x}_{i}=\\frac{6i}{n}$ and $f({x}_{i})={e}^{{x}_{i}}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{6i/n}\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $b=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-113918/ma-source-field/720717825c12e4ed3e6662ba6a7ebf4991022dba08ee332a513f78d45eaee733"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f663b0b-9b5e-512c-92bb-0ea84d5baac5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113918"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "4ed785a5-44c7-5d1c-ba4b-18ff8aed644c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "cce4d51d-668c-5887-ab39-f0222a35d908" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "706a81e0-fa08-57b0-b437-c2f1e80679af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "43a1fd11-acfb-51ce-8e45-54f73c52e999" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d/3157635cf9496371609f9768a1e617dfdac3f51d8fba589c5e495cb1c0105986" :answer/id #uuid "48b2153a-fd69-5239-a9c8-303b9cb48dd6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d" :answer-field/id #uuid "813feba2-b955-5d20-b059-a9fb82381546" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d/3157635cf9496371609f9768a1e617dfdac3f51d8fba589c5e495cb1c0105986"] :answer-field/correct "q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d/3157635cf9496371609f9768a1e617dfdac3f51d8fba589c5e495cb1c0105986" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122932" :question/id #uuid "d62099c6-5c34-55aa-ad1f-5500db9aeb0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122932" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-4,6]?$\n\nI. $-5<-4<-2<0<4<6$\nII. ${-3,3,5,6}$\nIII. ${-4,4,5}$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[-4,6]$ since $-5$ does not belong to $[-4,6].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-4,6]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=-4.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of  $[-4,6]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6].$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122932/ma-source-field/348fd3be69feefd43083733ebcc652d6128da4cf01d77dee32a483f066731f9d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122932"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7/068ab6c44549303840ef1adf9a99379c384e07623b26bb81c174d3bb8bd9009b" :answer/id #uuid "fcd4e9ae-e251-5b16-b1c3-5b9bc45cef41" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{n}$ and ${b}_{n}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7/05cd4bcc4cb0e269138afb0d66bb35f7af4dbde3de5e1c1069f015dacbc27a43" :answer/id #uuid "1c474915-3112-5a65-ba46-8702d62ab30b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{n}$ and ${c}_{n}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7/1023e9b710464a16063dd1eb1e93728db1cc8143fa56aa39ab69e81f77844de8" :answer/id #uuid "4bce095d-cbe6-5499-a685-c442389e61af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{n},$ ${b}_{n},$ and ${c}_{n}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7/8e921bffb50a4e46de83ddac3f98a24bb71d1e68ac0b40cb4fc363fa694725df" :answer/id #uuid "d4a0eaea-fc7b-55da-b356-f336150395ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${b}_{n}$ and ${c}_{n}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7/83b7363938f4c2d14a7a365d3c0c0baeb6dc576c6e844287a4a4a0fa6426f519" :answer/id #uuid "0b06ae43-fe31-53fd-8b10-6540097b006e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${c}_{n}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7" :answer-field/id #uuid "520b0925-7644-5da3-a57b-98c58f41393e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7/068ab6c44549303840ef1adf9a99379c384e07623b26bb81c174d3bb8bd9009b" "q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7/05cd4bcc4cb0e269138afb0d66bb35f7af4dbde3de5e1c1069f015dacbc27a43" "q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7/1023e9b710464a16063dd1eb1e93728db1cc8143fa56aa39ab69e81f77844de8" "q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7/8e921bffb50a4e46de83ddac3f98a24bb71d1e68ac0b40cb4fc363fa694725df" "q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7/83b7363938f4c2d14a7a365d3c0c0baeb6dc576c6e844287a4a4a0fa6426f519"] :answer-field/correct "q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7/1023e9b710464a16063dd1eb1e93728db1cc8143fa56aa39ab69e81f77844de8" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123715" :question/id #uuid "b9bf7b26-4c35-5b3c-bd82-2290add25e67" :question/math-academy-id "q-123715" :question/problem "Which of the following sequences, defined for $n\\ge 1,$ converge?\n\n- ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(3n)}{{e}^{2n}}$\n- ${b}_{n}=\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡n}{\\sqrt{n}}$\n- ${c}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n}}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for large values of $n,$ we have\n\n$$\nn!≫{e}^{n}≫{n}^{m}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n),\n$$\n\nwhere $≫$ means \"much greater than,\" and $m>0.$\n\nTo find the limit of each sequence, we must evaluate them for $n\\to \\infty .$\n\nFor ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(3n)}{{e}^{2n}},$ both the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFor ${b}_{n}=\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡n}{\\sqrt{n}},$ both the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{b}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFor ${c}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n}},$ both the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{c}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"${a}_{n},$ ${b}_{n},$ and ${c}_{n}.$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-123715/ma-source-field/3e9cec0a5a7147188d19ae5529acb87adbf9eeff11b54cf9fd4ef7085b35dcb7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51d50237-f6cf-5c2d-b8d1-335378205a28"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123715"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "2f030092-da67-5e23-9fdb-56642eb1665c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "08b646ac-4e89-5442-9a96-fda0b2f79464" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437/f073cec77042b855fcc95ae59e5c07a0d566930857e27de8effde7dcda1f144f" :answer/id #uuid "94c121cc-a02d-5f14-83e4-a6c4f52c26fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" :answer/id #uuid "015a3916-4f00-5a67-a764-b51e236937f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "c378d3ab-a8f5-57f7-bc3c-e72ba32865fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc69c548-b178-59cf-a7e3-c85b144b3d40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" "q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" "q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437/f073cec77042b855fcc95ae59e5c07a0d566930857e27de8effde7dcda1f144f" "q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" "q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3"] :answer-field/correct "q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437/f073cec77042b855fcc95ae59e5c07a0d566930857e27de8effde7dcda1f144f" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181670" :question/id #uuid "0e72e5e7-5d89-539b-aadc-437975100b51" :question/math-academy-id "q-181670" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\n- $A={n\\in Z\\,:\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{2})=1}$\n- $B={q\\in Q\\,:\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{q\\pi }{2})=1}$\n- $C={x\\in R\\,:\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x\\pi }{2})=1}$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\nWe start by finding the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x\\pi }{2})=1$ for $x\\in R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x\\pi }{2} & =2m\\pi  \\\\ x & =4m,\\,m\\in Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets:\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the elements of $B$ for different values of $m,$ we have\n\n$$\nA={…,-4,0,4,8,…}.\n$$\n\n- The set $B$ is infinite. Since $A$ is infinite, and $A⊆B,$ it follows that $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Since $B$ is infinite, and $B⊆C,$ it follows that $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-181670/ma-source-field/f18564ad9cd410b8b09b86bbb6efd0f9da29c0c47ff1262c33395c6c26f75437"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f98332fd-e902-5390-a4d3-4e181ce97219"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181670"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186064618 :question/answer-fields 17592186061755] {:db/id "q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "b0a7e325-bb6e-50d6-8115-8a687cfd729f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b53f607f-c200-5ff6-8ced-e452dc4d4a4b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "ae1b3034-251a-59f4-b113-773134be1def" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "0481ca8b-da90-5343-99ae-63643fac6ed9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "dc8d5f4e-4f95-5ba3-ba2b-62b542d4c351" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0" :answer-field/id #uuid "041ff950-f3f8-5661-8897-41d87f43abe3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :answer-field/correct "q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "542cb4a0-6380-5eaf-91e8-44f9300f10c9"] :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ defined on the closed interval $\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le e,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The global maximum value is $\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$\nII. The global minimum value is $e-2$\nIII. The global minimum value is $2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=1-\\frac{2}{x},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n1-\\frac{2}{x}=0\\,⟹\\,x=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=2,$ and the endpoints $x=\\frac{1}{2},e$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2≈1.9 \\\\ f(2) & =2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2≈0.6 \\\\ f(e) & =e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e=e-2≈0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ so the global maximum is $\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(2)=2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ so the global minimum is $2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"I and III only.\"\n\n![](images/6c/6cc3ee476c8c5dc9e27051c990b184318147caffd2177b760074172fe5c667f6.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-22428/ma-source-field/b4a689f59d0ef6b92b4d3a5d2b9e96edf2a67acd1662db974315bb0e5e1041e0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6/c820fc75b83ab642062caecaa665e20c3efdace607db6b590468cae51c449859" :answer/id #uuid "53e9c955-42a6-5020-a355-eae4fe66d4c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f$ and $h$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6/3a3755feb1a05cec3176c3d2cc45a265049aa4bdd6b69f00387a116663369c21" :answer/id #uuid "813b9b1c-2e23-599a-bbed-341899317794" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f,g,$ and $h$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6/8179e352607fde1d20643aaf2dd5550f91f25ca3d0bbbef167f92cf9dc7a168e" :answer/id #uuid "4c4fa032-2148-54c2-9c32-cbe3a90719b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$g$ and $h$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6/54260034644bf2398d955582fcfe14cc95cc4887ad666376368d8327ed5e3102" :answer/id #uuid "43827749-fd32-5ade-b947-0ae8c476e27e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$g$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6/2a1d8a89f00ace1b1ddd51d9e5ff705929e76b6edeee97f394d666550954368a" :answer/id #uuid "70a234cb-554b-545b-99a9-38ca1d4a7d30" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$h$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "7aedcafb-9859-554f-b742-1fe94afe482b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6/c820fc75b83ab642062caecaa665e20c3efdace607db6b590468cae51c449859" "q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6/3a3755feb1a05cec3176c3d2cc45a265049aa4bdd6b69f00387a116663369c21" "q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6/8179e352607fde1d20643aaf2dd5550f91f25ca3d0bbbef167f92cf9dc7a168e" "q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6/54260034644bf2398d955582fcfe14cc95cc4887ad666376368d8327ed5e3102" "q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6/2a1d8a89f00ace1b1ddd51d9e5ff705929e76b6edeee97f394d666550954368a"] :answer-field/correct "q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6/3a3755feb1a05cec3176c3d2cc45a265049aa4bdd6b69f00387a116663369c21" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341642" :question/id #uuid "4689ffaf-d7a6-5ea0-9161-3ec67ff19338" :question/math-academy-id "q-341642" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are piecewise continuous on $x\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\sqrt{x+1},\\,g(x)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & ⌈x⌉\\text{ is even} \\\\ -1,\\, & ⌈x⌉\\text{ is odd},\\end{aligned}\\,h(x)=u(x-1)+u\\,(x-\\frac{5}{2})+u(x-4).\n$$\n\nNote that $u(x)$ is the unit step function, and $⌈x⌉$ is the ceiling function." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $I⊆R.$ A function $f:I\\to R$ is piecewise continuous on $I$ if it is piecewise continuous on every closed and bounded subinterval $[a,b]⊂I.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty ).$ The function is continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The function $g(x)$ is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty ).$ The function has jump discontinuities at $x=0,1,2,…,$ and any closed interval $[a,b]⊂[0,\\infty )$ will contain finitely many discontinuities.\n\n![](images/d5/d5a497337426dad07096702a3e211f525a959add8cb1fbaaef05fccac26d634b.png)\n\n- The function $h(x)$ is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty )$ since it is continuous over $x\\in [0,\\infty )$ except at the points $x=1,$ $x=\\frac{5}{2},$ and $x=4,$ where the one-sided limits exist and are finite:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}h(x)=0,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}h(x)=1\n$$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 5/{2}^{-}}h(x)=1,\\,{lim}_{x\\to 5/{2}^{+}}h(x)=2\n$$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}h(x)=2,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}h(x)=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$f,g,$ and $h.$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341642/ma-source-field/0b42a35cf9155d6c8839d19a08f7feaf380c1d16addc0ea78abfd8950ff2a8d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5985dfc1-a05b-5ac9-a33d-8398478e252c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341642"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186115889 :question/answer-fields 17592186114241] {:db/id "q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558/263f2834c39a884ed4107d93e45891bf1c03e1239f1b605574fb2a4e7fa704de" :answer/id #uuid "f7475fa2-2dfb-5ab6-af30-4b6beda786d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-2$ and $x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558/caa1480127d61a1777b06d605f1adffc9022d9830425fbcfd75797676392e878" :answer/id #uuid "edc154f2-6797-5d5a-be28-0f6a1f59d668" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558/4cd3794b4d40064eb1b0b9373d288135b6006eb6017a90620f33df89464a261d" :answer/id #uuid "1541152a-7611-5c14-a588-d1e5cc5e22df" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-2$, $x=0$, and $x=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer/id #uuid "453cb038-db89-5863-98ef-ba1dcdd04c12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" :answer/id #uuid "6f7c45a8-6d0f-5a1d-b8dc-4e8e1b4b6ce1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558" :answer-field/id #uuid "71e2164a-d23d-528c-85fa-147024e56737" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558/263f2834c39a884ed4107d93e45891bf1c03e1239f1b605574fb2a4e7fa704de" "q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558/caa1480127d61a1777b06d605f1adffc9022d9830425fbcfd75797676392e878" "q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558/4cd3794b4d40064eb1b0b9373d288135b6006eb6017a90620f33df89464a261d" "q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" "q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042"] :answer-field/correct "q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558/4cd3794b4d40064eb1b0b9373d288135b6006eb6017a90620f33df89464a261d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "097f3e11-2ce8-55f7-bbfa-1640ee282b68"] :question/problem "![](images/8e/8e7daf95fadbe2262a09e8183f00d63075655f3b97dd363984c192ac3414ad17.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?" :question/worked-solution "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=-2$ the function has a cusp, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=0$ the function has a jump discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=2$ the function has an infinite discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-2$, $x=0$, and $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47650/ma-source-field/755e5b752eb9d2d2f547b6466c9b0c447faec7cf0b4ebcd497ca12ec9db32558"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186069374 :question/answer-fields 17592186067384] {:db/id "q-48080/ma-source-field/3d78c07082396065a839c356e147caa3a379154b66179782f9457f81a290b1e2/0be40a41fff2075dcd7ae30d0e6284ddf7b2ec7e519882e4636a79e6edbe7cee" :answer/id #uuid "e9d17f27-11e4-5d07-bef6-23b79d1c374c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48080/ma-source-field/3d78c07082396065a839c356e147caa3a379154b66179782f9457f81a290b1e2/f2099ec612a8ba2ad1232fc0698fe5c14c2ca2169a9927b8ddd0c140cf8bf767" :answer/id #uuid "e25593d7-0095-53cf-b3dd-44c1e9a1bd39" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-2$ and $x=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48080/ma-source-field/3d78c07082396065a839c356e147caa3a379154b66179782f9457f81a290b1e2/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer/id #uuid "a59fc894-dd6b-5b7f-b8bc-d6156ee4de53" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48080/ma-source-field/3d78c07082396065a839c356e147caa3a379154b66179782f9457f81a290b1e2/ab63e789ad10d34c2ff41e36a494d8b1a65dadbef60dc438a2edd1b43cabc88a" :answer/id #uuid "fb712dc7-5f7d-5b94-ab66-e243d5ea0505" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48080/ma-source-field/3d78c07082396065a839c356e147caa3a379154b66179782f9457f81a290b1e2/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" :answer/id #uuid "51dfca4a-207b-5033-87d0-8f1fd9a9fe6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48080/ma-source-field/3d78c07082396065a839c356e147caa3a379154b66179782f9457f81a290b1e2" :answer-field/id #uuid "17b83f56-ed58-5b0c-a67a-c211740c88f2" :answ