8e8b95f14cd/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" "q-335445/ma-source-field/4963854d5738bb7dd0ab55444b5272c502bab51af75df875ffdb88e8b95f14cd/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" "q-335445/ma-source-field/4963854d5738bb7dd0ab55444b5272c502bab51af75df875ffdb88e8b95f14cd/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68"] :answer-field/correct "q-335445/ma-source-field/4963854d5738bb7dd0ab55444b5272c502bab51af75df875ffdb88e8b95f14cd/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445" :question/id #uuid "ac4293b7-4265-5467-bc7b-b86d5611daed" :question/math-academy-id "q-335445" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=2+{e}^{-x},$ then $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O(2+{e}^{-x})$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}=0$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,{e}^{-x}=O(2)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(2)$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(1)$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-2}}  \nand  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property. \n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O({{2+{e}^{-x}}_{⏟}}_{f}),\n$$\n\nand this is true by the $\\text{reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(2+{e}^{-x}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\n{e}^{-x}=O(2).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines   $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and the  $\\text{absorption property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(2).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L4},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(2)\n$$\n\nand by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ with $c=2,$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(1).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335445/ma-source-field/8b1cea60124f7907edeaaa488e8258e3b70ebf1aca2f1f655e978ff6050fa208" "q-335445/ma-source-field/ff31020b1dffb99810a55331ac561e2ad11bec3980ea3d353555083bc19fbbca" "q-335445/ma-source-field/42d0b6fef1f1aaa0a59f05f6ccd1027dae593b1a8f3c849e15739680a4a7b745" "q-335445/ma-source-field/1e4c698b65d2df25ad42635339af80a80acdacd1ddaf95dcb3c6f8682f174260" "q-335445/ma-source-field/4963854d5738bb7dd0ab55444b5272c502bab51af75df875ffdb88e8b95f14cd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe4292f-7653-5486-975e-c206acae734e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335445"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335460/ma-source-field/44df59e4b9ee60c06dc2e1c10402131b446a935d930b385722eb315bc9eaa22b/e1381ae7c7a92b4aa7f0a2bd7d1adabb4c69d577c3ac304b32f6f859826b96b8" :answer/id #uuid "3edfa3a9-5202-50e5-bd72-0e10a5d47289" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335460/ma-source-field/44df59e4b9ee60c06dc2e1c10402131b4