f1628" :answer/id #uuid "ce094f55-879b-5b96-bedb-c8a97168bac2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/ma-source-field/1ab967f49acd08b3ec1c435f8ac83f0b4d52c32969e34a548062a1cecfc45577/d2d3ad1a05b61aef1bc2922f5a8427ad6e95e86a67e4f7cfa4a496e247409004" :answer/id #uuid "cccff4fe-20c3-5cb7-9681-92cc25121511" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477/ma-source-field/1ab967f49acd08b3ec1c435f8ac83f0b4d52c32969e34a548062a1cecfc45577" :answer-field/id #uuid "62e5d724-e4aa-50ec-8d98-2ca352e011f4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-336477/ma-source-field/1ab967f49acd08b3ec1c435f8ac83f0b4d52c32969e34a548062a1cecfc45577/314a8bf3988f29de8fd66f4fbfe199e21705e2d339ca177314f13a77b18830f3" "q-336477/ma-source-field/1ab967f49acd08b3ec1c435f8ac83f0b4d52c32969e34a548062a1cecfc45577/f3a9d801ccdd6cc1c09cebcca8041cf8701bcfc1cf625c969828c0ba6bc74018" "q-336477/ma-source-field/1ab967f49acd08b3ec1c435f8ac83f0b4d52c32969e34a548062a1cecfc45577/bccd64dc374427e0f7de51fbe3eab59b8bddd08872451dd6790ce294ecff1628" "q-336477/ma-source-field/1ab967f49acd08b3ec1c435f8ac83f0b4d52c32969e34a548062a1cecfc45577/d2d3ad1a05b61aef1bc2922f5a8427ad6e95e86a67e4f7cfa4a496e247409004"] :answer-field/correct "q-336477/ma-source-field/1ab967f49acd08b3ec1c435f8ac83f0b4d52c32969e34a548062a1cecfc45577/bccd64dc374427e0f7de51fbe3eab59b8bddd08872451dd6790ce294ecff1628" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336477" :question/id #uuid "b476f440-04ac-55c0-bbfe-8012f8f71f27" :question/math-academy-id "q-336477" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$  \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by  {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by substitution from lines {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from $\\text{L2},$ we have the identity\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c.\n$$\n\nEvaluating this identity at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L3}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{evaluating both sides at }t=0.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ From $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nand from $\\text{L4}$ we know ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={I}_{n}c=c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L5}.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{substituting }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}\\text{ into }x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$, $\\text{L2},$ $\\text{L5},$ and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L1}$ we have ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At},$ and from $\\text{L5}$ we know $c=x(0).$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ (line $\\text{L2}$), we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336477/ma-source-field/ddbc081bae0e4abdcf3785e792a38b1af6c850ae2b722c4d91c1395f89d943a2" "q-336477/ma-source-field/b1cc5428c04b6c2cf27b5113b81952ad4a5566cce03219942c5f59ad5178ec75" "q-336477/ma-source-field/1ab967f49acd08b3ec1c435f8ac83f0b4d52c32969e34a548062a1cecfc45577"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336477"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186167268 :question/answer-fields 17592186164762] {:db/id "q-336711/ma-source-field/f798d9da636a0660f9663a8ff4da79320516aca57140744faa214f9135f0b5fd/04d069a44bdfcbb7aeea2e3413cbeb8ec2d1c716ba6f3d2468c7908c9cee7685" :answer/id #uuid "3dd43670-1646-534f-9b82-0ec4c2ab4066" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/ma-source-field/f798d9da636a0660f9663a8ff4da79320516aca57140744faa214f9135f0b5fd/d1aa86a131a1ca96e44bba21e54e2732575b1dbe4a9dbe6bd49933ee371c6148" :answer/id #uuid "0314521e-1ee3-553c-a49a-28490b5dc131" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/ma-source-field/f798d9da636a0660f9663a8ff4da79320516aca57140744faa214f9135f0b5fd/08a383c0cd6483e92e91f2b1657bbc1cdf0d1ef2b71cc1c1a15f81f328755bb8" :answer/id #uuid "fabeb164-e1c7-5722-8dd4-7476a0c9cdb3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "integrating" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/ma-source-field/f798d9da636a0660f9663a8ff4da79320516aca57140744faa214f9135f0b5fd/fb83a2a64257fd0db88480cbbfbfd15880d454885b303b14c12196ffa9d196ac" :answer/id #uuid "b70f4cdd-82f4-5102-b82d-3bb67d075165" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/ma-source-field/f798d9da636a0660f9663a8ff4da79320516aca5714