id "q-336711/ma-source-field/5577360ed4c88de6ff84d89daf778f555c25e11e0b906236b6d49834517e28d7/ccf76eebdf7ce9ae0b5dde3aebd52f96b8d0ace039e4f3840066eb7bdceffda5" :answer/id #uuid "7b292260-1158-5bf9-8ff9-6e83083ce40c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ is an invertible" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/ma-source-field/5577360ed4c88de6ff84d89daf778f555c25e11e0b906236b6d49834517e28d7/fe58f15b437f419a568483c3d2a3a7f47a19ceac31d0be0d5089eba1dda34ced" :answer/id #uuid "0e5ac2ca-d399-5fa8-b244-bbd050e7ea77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ is the identity" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/ma-source-field/5577360ed4c88de6ff84d89daf778f555c25e11e0b906236b6d49834517e28d7/3d708aa1d08f986166eb15c8c8b055c2417252bca2d1b161dbd272f31e6e2d1e" :answer/id #uuid "73fc77df-9183-5392-9f5f-84c6b7225cb0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/ma-source-field/5577360ed4c88de6ff84d89daf778f555c25e11e0b906236b6d49834517e28d7/608ecd34b8f8740cb8effac004d7b7e1ed9d320555e152e568ed0eb9a2bf48e7" :answer/id #uuid "33ab2692-3bf2-5c51-81e7-2d7540647496" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Φ$ is a square" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336711/ma-source-field/5577360ed4c88de6ff84d89daf778f555c25e11e0b906236b6d49834517e28d7" :answer-field/id #uuid "369c338a-25f1-56f5-856e-c6afcea5d80e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-336711/ma-source-field/5577360ed4c88de6ff84d89daf778f555c25e11e0b906236b6d49834517e28d7/ccf76eebdf7ce9ae0b5dde3aebd52f96b8d0ace039e4f3840066eb7bdceffda5" "q-336711/ma-source-field/5577360ed4c88de6ff84d89daf778f555c25e11e0b906236b6d49834517e28d7/fe58f15b437f419a568483c3d2a3a7f47a19ceac31d0be0d5089eba1dda34ced" "q-336711/ma-source-field/5577360ed4c88de6ff84d89daf778f555c25e11e0b906236b6d49834517e28d7/3d708aa1d08f986166eb15c8c8b055c2417252bca2d1b161dbd272f31e6e2d1e" "q-336711/ma-source-field/5577360ed4c88de6ff84d89daf778f555c25e11e0b906236b6d49834517e28d7/608ecd34b8f8740cb8effac004d7b7e1ed9d320555e152e568ed0eb9a2bf48e7"] :answer-field/correct "q-336711/ma-source-field/5577360ed4c88de6ff84d89daf778f555c25e11e0b906236b6d49834517e28d7/3d708aa1d08f986166eb15c8c8b055c2417252bca2d1b161dbd272f31e6e2d1e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "f3e98464-6e85-513e-a930-d0947c1c72b6"] :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}} both sides of  the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-4}} matrix." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ To get $\\text{L2},$ we are $\\text{differentiating}$ with respect to $t$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =(Φu(t))^{′} \\\\ {x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Let's substitute ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$ from $\\text{L1}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into $\\text{initial system of ODEs}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{pre-multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $c(t)$ of $Φ$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n{c}^{′}(t)=Ac(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}^{′}(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $Φ.$ As a result, this means that ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that $Φ\\text{ is a fundamental}$ matrix." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336711/ma-source-field/f798d9da636a0660f9663a8ff4da79320516aca57140744faa214f9135f0b5fd" "q-336711/ma-source-field/39fe76f05e07737b3104b66025465ff05bc05c40460b1f1d4d223b24d021fb32" "q-336711/ma-source-field/93e9ecda50df29ff898c1fb6193aff9fb63d8713cea99e1cac26ce8907c288b1" "q-336711/ma-source-field/5577360ed4c88de6ff84d89daf778f555c25e11e0b906236b6d49834517e28d7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-336716/ma-source-field/f798d9da636a0660f9663a8ff4da7