9bcfca775d3a68c8dbda3488530fcdbc4e655456b1b9c2023f/f06a8441c4bec30e864c6c39be6abf4457946a31c6a745cafe755726146ff770" :answer/id #uuid "c8a52c32-4263-5deb-99be-91d902304f59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336716/ma-source-field/b204a0c9f18ce89bcfca775d3a68c8dbda3488530fcdbc4e655456b1b9c2023f" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa75475c-51ab-516a-9842-72a619727da2" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-336716/ma-source-field/b204a0c9f18ce89bcfca775d3a68c8dbda3488530fcdbc4e655456b1b9c2023f/042168976629a933b0d0ef460bdad0013cb33b8a34cdbca393ce80067da1046d" "q-336716/ma-source-field/b204a0c9f18ce89bcfca775d3a68c8dbda3488530fcdbc4e655456b1b9c2023f/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" "q-336716/ma-source-field/b204a0c9f18ce89bcfca775d3a68c8dbda3488530fcdbc4e655456b1b9c2023f/124b0c2eb11420d91f7684989e46375a3c1c904a04910b2d823439550b297bf2" "q-336716/ma-source-field/b204a0c9f18ce89bcfca775d3a68c8dbda3488530fcdbc4e655456b1b9c2023f/f06a8441c4bec30e864c6c39be6abf4457946a31c6a745cafe755726146ff770"] :answer-field/correct "q-336716/ma-source-field/b204a0c9f18ce89bcfca775d3a68c8dbda3488530fcdbc4e655456b1b9c2023f/042168976629a933b0d0ef460bdad0013cb33b8a34cdbca393ce80067da1046d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336716" :question/id #uuid "68ae00aa-e57d-5620-9c00-ead6febaac73" :question/math-academy-id "q-336716" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}} both sides of  the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting {{field-3}} into {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ To get $\\text{L2},$ we are $\\text{differentiating}$ with respect to $t$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =(Φu(t))^{′} \\\\ {x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L7},$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336716/ma-source-field/f798d9da636a0660f9663a8ff4da79320516aca57140744faa214f9135f0b5fd" "q-336716/ma-source-field/3ff7a09d434d29f5b81bfe5a2bd4f82633716e302fff8a1900dd9d3a3ad5b787" "q-336716/ma-source-field/9d1303aed8395b41