question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y={e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+4{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-4x})}^{′}+4(u{e}^{-4x}) & ={e}^{-4x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-4u{e}^{-4x}+4u{e}^{-4x} & ={e}^{-4x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-\\cancel{4u{e}^{-4x}}+\\cancel{4u{e}^{-4x}} & ={e}^{-4x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x} & ={e}^{-4x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =1 \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-4x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-4x} \\\\  & =x{e}^{-4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337466/ma-source-field/9f656a9e2c8340f3d3b6f4ecae919de5556902dddce5436638c2dfe75e50d2a9" "q-337466/ma-source-field/ef47a4908d120c047cccd7ca2dab447ff02eefbaee8519012f780b2053efaaa8" "q-337466/ma-source-field/51eb84176c384cf4a279fae06a2962fae6351ac9e1ce45fccd292cdb0bf3b4b4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337466"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337469/ma-source-field/4adfba6e2eab8ea14a33b1abd4e02de59b12a7a74e6367e98b30bcd7a4ebb416/0f0bf3e5b4d49d098cc5baf660c6977edc9ec113af6f735d59f497de50943951" :answer/id #uuid "a584cd0d-27c6-531c-970d-493932778886" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337469/ma-source-field/4adfba6e2eab8ea14a33b1abd4e02de59b12a7a74e6367e98b30bcd7a4ebb416/0dfd7211371cc7d8403c054fcef962b61d8a8feaf3d34d77257754f397cd581b" :answer/id #uuid "79ff23f2-915d-5d8b-9114-3779b44c89bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337469/ma-source-field/4adfba6e2eab8ea14a33b1abd4e02de59b12a7a74e6367e98b30bcd7a4ebb416/b17bc55297fcfa21ff8825c4fc77e14e581b1d9e6ce116e901996f6ba2e38511" :answer/id #uuid "0124f381-e063-50ed-b5a1-3c3f9da3ad9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-7x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337469/ma-source-field/4adfba6e2eab8ea14a33b1abd4e02de59b12a7a74e6367e98b30bcd7a4ebb416/1c87915a6c57b766bbb06d9fd3b05c238a68caca6be59893391c9af122458273" :answer/id #uuid "38447498-29d3-5175-a4df-a73a990ee625" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337469/ma-source-field/4adfba6e2eab8ea14a33b1abd4e02de59b12a7a74e6367e98b30bcd7a4ebb416/e912f68733f4a80eee8575a72c55c20feffdc1726bceb2f5d1304999aac87760"