-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-337488/ma-source-field/a8ca88144c7493bf6acd07f32859897f075030bf3bb4f729e120260d5a8f63da/261b8ef6e8723a5a394c1097c9f18e472d66b4b97220048446e711330a0b0c95" "q-337488/ma-source-field/a8ca88144c7493bf6acd07f32859897f075030bf3bb4f729e120260d5a8f63da/f7e9c87fe4ecac4f8e31de701bf2a34ec5c5705a54baec247aaaa219d3e179ea" "q-337488/ma-source-field/a8ca88144c7493bf6acd07f32859897f075030bf3bb4f729e120260d5a8f63da/48ebb325525812d84be8e0c14f0aa66188310af1e9eaed985096f789d20492ee" "q-337488/ma-source-field/a8ca88144c7493bf6acd07f32859897f075030bf3bb4f729e120260d5a8f63da/0855fcc906a7b7b01a6613b4fb2373595586ed243f8262eaa74ec8742c15c9eb"] :answer-field/correct "q-337488/ma-source-field/a8ca88144c7493bf6acd07f32859897f075030bf3bb4f729e120260d5a8f63da/48ebb325525812d84be8e0c14f0aa66188310af1e9eaed985096f789d20492ee" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/ma-source-field/85c138f591db9c1cf6f4aa80dde47f8c27e59ec9f2fa7894ff011f212a3522aa/dd3378361514ba05f27e95e6befd7149234fafdfa6c0b12d143bc61c5e70723c" :answer/id #uuid "ba369324-b632-52dd-b087-db8abad2c3bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/ma-source-field/85c138f591db9c1cf6f4aa80dde47f8c27e59ec9f2fa7894ff011f212a3522aa/37177e90727d3601cb17824eef909face0cea78b2be953db134acaa24554c173" :answer/id #uuid "06d45bf0-b0d2-526d-9ee8-966bee2bf82f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x{e}^{5x}-{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/ma-source-field/85c138f591db9c1cf6f4aa80dde47f8c27e59ec9f2fa7894ff011f212a3522aa/9d3d0c12ff13c139e54d88e65e3903a204678f1298f7597091e06e6bf3a65fb3" :answer/id #uuid "cd83b01b-26af-5c69-90f0-dea06d731251" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/ma-source-field/85c138f591db9c1cf6f4aa80dde47f8c27e59ec9f2fa7894ff011f212a3522aa/4e7280cd22327c2ba538c3921b3cdfa1cf343e100e973b659982e51f6ffac664" :answer/id #uuid "f899948d-7d57-564f-9c17-dc1a4e8c1e4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5x}-x{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/ma-source-field/85c138f591db9c1cf6f4aa80dde47f8c27e59ec9f2fa7894ff011f212a3522aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "02bdb63b-0f09-5614-88a9-63938cc89b6d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-337488/ma-source-field/85c138f591db9c1cf6f4aa80dde47f8c27e59ec9f2fa7894ff011f212a3522aa/dd3378361514ba05f27e95e6befd7149234fafdfa6c0b12d143bc61c5e70723c" "q-337488/ma-source-field/85c138f591db9c1cf6f4aa80dde47f8c27e59ec9f2fa7894ff011f212a3522aa/37177e90727d3601cb17824eef909face0cea78b2be953db134acaa24554c173" "q-337488/ma-source-field/85c138f591db9c1cf6f4aa80dde47f8c27e59ec9f2fa7894ff011f212a3522aa/9d3d0c12ff13c139e54d88e65e3903a204678f1298f7597091e06e6bf3a65fb3" "q-337488/ma-source-field/85c138f591db9c1cf6f4aa80dde47f8c27e59ec9f2fa7894ff011f212a3522aa/4e7280cd22327c2ba538c3921b3cdfa1cf343e100e973b659982e51f6ffac664"] :answer-field/correct "q-337488/ma-source-field/85c138f591db9c1cf6f4aa80dde47f8c27e59ec9f2fa7894ff011f212a3522aa/dd3378361514ba05f27e95e6befd7149234fafdfa6c0b12d143bc61c5e70723c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488" :question/id #uuid "5bf23900-2f3d-53c0-9448-69b2b01a2a2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-337488" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y=10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{5x})}^{′}-5(u{e}^{5x}) & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+5u{e}^{5x}-5u{e}^{5x} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}}-\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′} & =10{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x=\\frac{{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}}{2}\n$$\n\nour equation for $u$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =10{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\  & =10{e}^{-5x}(\\frac{{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}}{2}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{-5x}({e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}) \\\\  & =5+5{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =5+5{e}^{-10x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5+5{e}^{-10x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =5x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{5x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{5x} \\\\  & =5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.