select :answer-field/choices ["q-338646/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" "q-338646/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9"] :answer-field/correct "q-338646/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186152582 :question/answer-fields 17592186149932] {:db/id "q-338646/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "d23b2ad9-78b8-5e2c-978b-06f7f0b9daca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338646/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer/id #uuid "0fde711e-fce0-537b-85be-fb90e2b76123" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338646/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148" :answer-field/id #uuid "f19326da-14c5-5131-a8ff-fcda659769b1" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-338646/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" "q-338646/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9"] :answer-field/correct "q-338646/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "dc19be1d-a106-5173-ab6a-0a0d552a59ea"] :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){y}^{′}(x)+3y(x)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 2\n$$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=-1\n$$\n\nComplete the missing information below:\n\n$\\,$ The governing differential equation is {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, the {{field-2}} boundary conditions are {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nA set of Dirichlet, Neumann, or Robin boundary conditions is homogeneous if both right-hand sides are zero (i.e., ${\\gamma }_{1}={\\gamma }_{2}=0.)$ Otherwise, they are inhomogeneous.\n\nA boundary value problem is homogeneous if the differential equation is homogeneous $(f≡0)$ and the corresponding boundary conditions are homogeneous. Otherwise, the BVP is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- The governing differential equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){y}^{′}(x)+3y(x)=0.\n$$\n\nSince the right-hand side $f(x)≡0,$ the equation is $\\text{homogeneous}.$\n\n- The boundary conditions are\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=-1.\n$$\n\nThese are $\\text{Neumann}$ boundary conditions, and since the right-hand sides are not zero for both, they are $\\text{inhomogeneous}.$\n\n- Since the governing equation is homogeneous, yet the boundary conditions are inhomogeneous, the BVP is $\\text{inhomogeneous}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338646/ma-source-field/659bc76d13d27aa09af5070fc47b0ed556b5af6ef8541f344a8c58e3f4f79515" "q-338646/ma-source-field/35076650840cbb6beacf9f343738a476a3e52b3aadd11f5ca9f98f5a2c7cbdce" "q-338646/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b" "q-338646/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186229727 :question/answer-fields 17592186228537] {:db/id "q-338682/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50/323c3707f259ac463f43078adb40da54bd6fbd62183256b458b52b49dc2a9da0" :answer/id #uuid "777c0bde-5c50-58aa-bcd9-af554298f662" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338682/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be968afd490c200de57c59561755" :answer/id #uuid "18bbb808-067a-5c73-a58a-7bbbccd30b52" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338682/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50" :answer-field/id #uuid "00839b4e-f62d-5523-b0a0-cd44b3f38d1f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-338682/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50/323c3707f259ac463f43078adb40da54bd6fbd62183256b458b52b49dc2a9da0" "q-338682/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be968afd490c200de57c59561755"] :answer-field/correct "q-338682/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be968afd490c200de57c59561755" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186229727 :question/answer-fields 17592186228540] {:db/id "q-338682/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589/d1f6c915b4e3a1496843bec633b4d1faefcdef0d6c86e2f095279d4c052efb98" :answer/id #uuid "3f94849a-be66-556b-b362-390c2fd77a3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338682/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589/ad5bfb9ccc3a6d948c3146ce91a4641b42b6fbd31026ea9a2acd2a98208ac3fa" :answer/id #uuid "4046271d-3273-5e3f-a757-9112f2fda282" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "sine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338682/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ef1e3c-f0e2-50af-90e8-066404b32b3d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-338682/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589/d1f6c915b4e3a1496843bec633b4d1faefcdef0d6c86e2f095279d4c052efb98" "q-338682/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589/ad5bfb9ccc3a6d948c3146ce91a4641b42b6fbd31026ea9a2acd2a98208ac3fa"] :answer-field/correct "q-338682/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589/d1f6c915b4e3a1496843bec633b4d1faefcdef0d6c86e2f095279d4c052efb98" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "d7903a61-d4e3-5a7b-991a-79f6efafb8b5"] :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the \n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ we have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${a}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{odd}$ and the $\\text{cosine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-338682/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50" "q-338682/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485/eacec3da0d49aa56b1d7012ab9e3dec997b7d12cbbba21f6dc41f1863d280a9a" :answer/id #uuid "b91b465b-5b4d-556f-8377-2a1cf46f49c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "det(A)=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485/1dac312fd2e4075f4a79dadb6cae2b8c6bb87c17456e84b37d0849b924588b48" :answer/id #uuid "6f1122a1-93f6-5c64-9f87-7969988c17b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "det(A)\\ne 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485" :answer-field/id #uuid "51dfa5bc-f977-5d9b-ba50-23229e7fd4f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-338686/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485/eacec3da0d49aa56b1d7012ab9e3dec997b7d12cbbba21f6dc41f1863d280a9a" "q-338686/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485/1dac312fd2e4075f4a79dadb6cae2b8c6bb87c17456e84b37d0849b924588b48"] :answer-field/correct "q-338686/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485/1dac312fd2e4075f4a79dadb6cae2b8c6bb87c17456e84b37d0849b924588b48" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686/ma-source-field/0bbacd3c3f753bf23c04cbae8da15b812667d606a3e3fbc6bd07478fcff89e33/a28d77d095ceb4216cf3d58cafd3052d249a86929d166d012c6ae491cfee0671" :answer/id #uuid "c741b2ff-ab7f-50e9-8510-a9245c14a314" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686/ma-source-field/0bbacd3c3f753bf23c04cbae8da15b812667d606a3e3fbc6bd07478fcff89e33/6391f4223570186cb06f9749b1ea5836a6ce6d24fca616cf7d80254149c12c5f" :answer/id #uuid "c42e4b6e-5657-51bb-8a20-e55e05bf0b4b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686/ma-source-field/0bbacd3c3f753bf23c04cbae8da15b812667d606a3e3fbc6bd07478fcff89e33/64353ef3a8a9aa2f99122e91ccb5d12440859fcfc37e667d5bd6bf246aa50fc3" :answer/id #uuid "8e6ce6c5-93bd-58b1-9fb8-00392e5ae9bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{2x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-x}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338686/ma-source-field/0bbacd3c3f753bf23c04cbae8da15b812667d606a3e3fbc6bd07478fcff89e33/df3e2eaf6d27caeb279bf3f0fc1e05dbdc785a92376d946c4a010d928c654e9c" :answer/id #uuid "c0522330-3e52-5790-9a75-e3f8ff7f852d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ an