swer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338700/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3fa453d-7107-5ec3-9427-f1bb56e42551" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-338700/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" "q-338700/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9"] :answer-field/correct "q-338700/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338700/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "e49e4968-19a7-5c51-82d4-60b6c4e6e37b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338700/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer/id #uuid "07be78c0-c60b-5a00-a83a-c253c5eb6a9c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338700/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148" :answer-field/id #uuid "91f26eb2-9af1-5ccb-a522-7f873fdb0095" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-338700/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" "q-338700/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9"] :answer-field/correct "q-338700/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338700" :question/id #uuid "748763ae-3cf4-5f3d-aa38-02f8044e2446" :question/math-academy-id "q-338700" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{y}^{′}(x)+y(x)=0,\\,-1\\le x\\le 1\n$$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=0\n$$\n\nComplete the missing information below:\n\n$\\,$ The governing differential equation is {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, the {{field-2}} boundary conditions are {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem is {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "For a second-order boundary value problem, \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y(x)=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x),Q(x)$ and $f(x)$ are all continuous on $[a,b],$ we have the following boundary condition classifications. \n\n- Dirichlet:\n\n$$\ny(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,y(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Neumann:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\n- Robin (mixed):\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\gamma }_{i},{\\alpha }_{i},$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real numbers with $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nA set of Dirichlet, Neumann, or Robin boundary conditions is homogeneous if both right-hand sides are zero (i.e., ${\\gamma }_{1}={\\gamma }_{2}=0.)$ Otherwise, they are inhomogeneous.\n\nA boundary value problem is homogeneous if the differential equation is homogeneous $(f≡0)$ and the corresponding boundary conditions are homogeneous. Otherwise, the BVP is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- The governing differential equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,{y}^{′}(x)+y(x)=0.\n$$\n\nSince the right-hand side $f(x)≡0,$ the equation is $\\text{homogeneous}.$\n\n- The boundary conditions are\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=0.\n$$\n\nThese are $\\text{Neumann}$ boundary conditions, and since the right-hand sides are not zero for both, they are $\\text{inhomogeneous}.$\n\n- Since the governing equation is homogeneous, yet the boundary conditions are inhomogeneous, the BVP is $\\text{inhomogeneous}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338700/ma-source-field/659bc76d13d27aa09af5070fc47b0ed556b5af6ef8541f344a8c58e3f4f79515" "q-338700/ma-source-field/35076650840cbb6beacf9f343738a476a3e52b3aadd11f5ca9f98f5a2c7cbdce" "q-338700/ma-source-field/bc70985f4d012f18ce462b781b455e47316d7d62e5bc1c56f480dd63a33c059b" "q-338700/ma-source-field/947acceff23d77d1e11fd7a62cf60c6e87947d113418ca9fc39a3f66bd026148"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af8cf798-4327-5f5b-82ab-f622f20ccc38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338700"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338713/ma-source-field/b416211afb1db3691dc69bd37b794a6a12159a613c3c04f5654bced2573a228d/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7" :answer/id #uuid "2636ba5a-474e-5a5d-9cb3-c2f759834dd5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "homogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338713/ma-source-field/b416211afb1db3691dc69bd37b794a6a12159a613c3c04f5654bced2573a228d/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" :answer/id #uuid "da6fc2f4-1dc3-536a-a5eb-cd6619ddf024" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "inhomogeneous" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338713/ma-source-field/b416211afb1db3691dc69bd37b794a6a12159a613c3c04f5654bced2573a228d" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5c9b5ab-10e3-5417-9498-0531c5e83157" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-3387