swer/id #uuid "86e0f9bf-00a1-5204-9647-0bc6ec485936" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{B}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3{\\lambda }_{n}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338907/ma-source-field/8364847892a8957be9bdf9e77d2f3699a0d8a120ff95a2f1d21fbc60498e8c56/381885b8433e26ab8892b24eada4bbc8a65c4e3b705bb6cccab7f8ebde202844" :answer/id #uuid "d149f557-f909-5ed0-be99-174185a4e256" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{B}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{{\\lambda }_{n}x}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338907/ma-source-field/8364847892a8957be9bdf9e77d2f3699a0d8a120ff95a2f1d21fbc60498e8c56/4c7f9b00f6a5d524498f88a0a58d9bc65fc00e5bddc1dedfc2e00fdfa3fd4de9" :answer/id #uuid "15092485-4594-5a18-ac64-9c22f0bd52ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{B}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({\\lambda }_{n}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338907/ma-source-field/8364847892a8957be9bdf9e77d2f3699a0d8a120ff95a2f1d21fbc60498e8c56" :answer-field/id #uuid "57b058f9-2857-5bd3-9ddc-d9ffd448c64e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-338907/ma-source-field/8364847892a8957be9bdf9e77d2f3699a0d8a120ff95a2f1d21fbc60498e8c56/aeaf24b48d279042afe82f3c96de006a764235e753373757b70e01af0a1912f7" "q-338907/ma-source-field/8364847892a8957be9bdf9e77d2f3699a0d8a120ff95a2f1d21fbc60498e8c56/4a75e9a2e5bfd13a12447f57bc02cf71af72ed34c01dd6738e450507c1ebec9b" "q-338907/ma-source-field/8364847892a8957be9bdf9e77d2f3699a0d8a120ff95a2f1d21fbc60498e8c56/c66d12940b08a4c8652c5eb6e3c4a0a42e7250e1bf3eaa0baedcc2741c2d606f" "q-338907/ma-source-field/8364847892a8957be9bdf9e77d2f3699a0d8a120ff95a2f1d21fbc60498e8c56/ca7b13a5940dff36f08e8a3f527da1e4f852ccea59b5a2daf4e1d4c0286d1435" "q-338907/ma-source-field/8364847892a8957be9bdf9e77d2f3699a0d8a120ff95a2f1d21fbc60498e8c56/381885b8433e26ab8892b24eada4bbc8a65c4e3b705bb6cccab7f8ebde202844" "q-338907/ma-source-field/8364847892a8957be9bdf9e77d2f3699a0d8a120ff95a2f1d21fbc60498e8c56/4c7f9b00f6a5d524498f88a0a58d9bc65fc00e5bddc1dedfc2e00fdfa3fd4de9"] :answer-field/correct "q-338907/ma-source-field/8364847892a8957be9bdf9e77d2f3699a0d8a120ff95a2f1d21fbc60498e8c56/ca7b13a5940dff36f08e8a3f527da1e4f852ccea59b5a2daf4e1d4c0286d1435" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338907" :question/id #uuid "958d5083-ae6b-5fcf-874a-f964110a9edf" :question/math-academy-id "q-338907" :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9{\\lambda }^{2}y=0,\\,y(0)=y(\\pi )=0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem.$\\,$ The eigenvalues correspond to the parameter values ${\\lambda }_{n}=$ {{field-1}}, where $n\\in N.$\n\n$\\,$ The eigenfunctions are ${y}_{n}(x)=$ {{field-2}}, where ${B}_{n}\\in R.$" :question/worked-solution "We consider the cases $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda \\ne 0$ separately, since they correspond to different solutions. \n\n**Case 1**: First, we consider $\\lambda =0.$ \n\nSetting $\\lambda =0$ gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrating this equation gives\n\n$$\ny=Ax+B.\n$$\n\nApplying the conditions $y(0)=y(\\pi )=0$ yields the trivial solution $y≡0.$ Since the zero solution is not an eigenfunction, $\\lambda =0$ does not correspond to an eigenvalue.\n\n**Case 2**: Next, we consider $\\lambda >0.$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+9{\\lambda }^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm 3\\text{i}\\lambda .$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\lambda x),\\,{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\lambda x)\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\lambda x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\lambda x).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(0)=0$ yields\n\n$$\nA\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)=0\n$$\n\nwhich gives $A=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\ny=B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\lambda x).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(\\pi )=0$ yields\n\n$$\nB\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\lambda \\pi )=0.\n$$\n\nFor nontrivial solutions, we require \n\n$$\n3\\lambda \\pi =n\\pi \n$$\n\nfor $n\\in N.$ This gives the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{n}=\\frac{n}{3}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding eigenfunctions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{n}(x)={B}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3{\\lambda }_{n}x),\\,{B}_{n}\\in R.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338907/ma-source-field/7d0be646b763c7efa8349c7c91b90522bea6c601f9d2d628f8949390818ea2e9" "q-338907/ma-source-field/8364847892a8957be9bdf9e77d2f3699a0d8a120ff95a2f1d21fbc60498e8c56"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "472cbb79-e22b-50d2-a997-93130ff66c22"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338907"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338982/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485/eacec3da0d49aa56b1d7012ab9e3dec997b7d12cbbba21f6dc41f1863d280a9a" :answer/id #uuid "3900c0eb-6950-53f9-bfb1-9594df80a763" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "det(A)=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338982/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485/1dac312fd2e4075f4a79dadb6cae2b8c6bb87c17456e84b37d0849b924588b48" :answer/id #uuid "dcc04b9a-9cfc-5141-a860-86088f43169c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "det(A)\\ne 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338982/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485" :answer-field/id #uuid "40ecf88c-bee2-552d-9e9b-2221a6455c26" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-338982/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485/eacec3da0d49aa56b1d7012ab9e3dec997b7d12cbbba21f6dc41f1863d280a9a" "q-338982/ma-source-fi