.type/text :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488/3cca3fa3537838e6a5d0d30fe92c8c8eeb37955af9a5daddd94e58b9528ef66c" :answer/id #uuid "7ecfede9-c62d-5886-a299-f1a637666f1c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "has no solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488/0b7fd52e1c7f46b2ed74642e86de045ddeb474ed53503764d8a67bbfe9b7fea8" :answer/id #uuid "fc9b72e9-fff2-5f3d-af71-a6cc5a8690e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "has the unique solution $y≡0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c637c93-1ee3-58ef-993c-3c6e5c1fc84b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488/21db0c8ca9c465ab3726d776a7cb92cb1c12957887d4f2cf603108bedfebbf8a" "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488/3cca3fa3537838e6a5d0d30fe92c8c8eeb37955af9a5daddd94e58b9528ef66c" "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488/0b7fd52e1c7f46b2ed74642e86de045ddeb474ed53503764d8a67bbfe9b7fea8"] :answer-field/correct "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488/0b7fd52e1c7f46b2ed74642e86de045ddeb474ed53503764d8a67bbfe9b7fea8" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338982" :question/id #uuid "76fbcb9f-680c-51b9-b052-efdce55007dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-338982" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+3y=0,\\,y(1)={y}^{′}(3)=0,\\,1\\le x\\le 3\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ be the fundamental solutions, and suppose we define the matrix $A$ as \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}(1) & {y}_{2}(1) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′}(3) & {y}_{2}^{′}(3)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFill in the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem has a unique solution if and only if {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The fundamental solutions to this BVP are {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, we have $det(A)=$ {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, this BVP {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have the second-order homogeneous boundary value (BVP) problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y=0,\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwith the Robin (mixed) boundary conditions\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)=0,\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ and $Q$ are continuous on $[a,b],$ and ${\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i}$ are real constants such that $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ Furthermore, suppose the fundamental solutions to the equation are ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$   \n\nNow, let's define the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{1}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}(a) & {\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{2}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}(a) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{1}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}(b) & {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{2}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}(b)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the BVP has a unique, trivial solution $y≡0$ if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\nIn other words, if the determinant equals zero, then the BVP has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nNotice that, in our case, we have Robin boundary conditions given by\n\n$$\ny(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(3)=0.\n$$\n\nSo, setting ${\\alpha }_{1}=1,$ ${\\beta }_{1}=0,$ ${\\alpha }_{2}=0,$ ${\\beta }_{2}=1,$ and $a=1,$ $b=3,$ the matrix $A$ reduces to\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}(1) & {y}_{2}(1) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′}(3) & {y}_{2}^{′}(3)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-4m+3 & =0 \\\\ (m-1)(m-3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have ${m}_{1}=1$ and ${m}_{2}=3,$ and so the fundamental solutions are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}\\,\\text{and}\\,{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{′}(x)={e}^{x},\\,{y}_{2}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{1} & {e}^{3(1)} \\\\ {e}^{3} & 3{e}^{3(3)}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}e & {e}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{3} & 3{e}^{9}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =e(3{e}^{9})-{e}^{3}({e}^{3}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{10}-{e}^{6} \\\\  & ={e}^{6}(3{e}^{4}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that this BVP $\\text{has the unique solution }y≡0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338982/ma-source-field/460df79cff40da171f2eb21459855b4edf560c36fb557923f0a716c043ddf485" "q-338982/ma-source-field/bbf154adee8f0ae4bad077f4defb7855896bbb5b4a9db96754635faa307e4a70" "q-338982/ma-source-field/43a35218b1cf23450e4e061cffa2a4a6e8e5b1bbad2021d4dc7405327bcce8f2" "q-338982/ma-source-field/07635e4aae3ceb82946a6de76931aa2924a7e32991119c72eb82b846bcc05488"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d9576e0-3be5-5d05-8cc8-c3ecde496b46"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338982"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" :answer/id #uuid "ddaeb121-e0a6-501b-9a51-af6c7d17b5d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda/077e9e54179703601a4dd3177dbc11815994aa839a7d7d5b12c3e1ec39527ef2" :answer/id #uuid "4e829349-3bd7-53b1-81eb-45b5da9870a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{12x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda/8d5d023c3a301fb9a8d23477feea46f05f0d5405aee5f9b110d5b86d86e2e4dd" :answer/id #uuid "327e9b36-504a-55cd-bdeb-9a295dbac872" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda/3341f139f0ee0d62d8758bd01e1eedd529e55f6b927830ec42423f0a16d137a0" :answer/id #uuid "831b7918-1f4b-50de-b1bd-28a0091624cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1cc20f5-acca-5b79-8f90-bd4ac033d4c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda/192c6030d8816553cdfcf13c7f5f26bd0bc0f29788b453b1e64332880bc35044" "q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda/077e9e54179703601a4dd3177dbc11815994aa839a7d7d5b12c3e1ec39527ef2" "q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda/8d5d023c3a301fb9a8d23477feea46f05f0d5405aee5f9b110d5b86d86e2e4dd" "q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda/3341f139f0ee0d62d8758bd01e1eedd529e55f6b927830ec42423f0a16d137a0"] :answer-field/correct "q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda/8d5d023c3a301fb9a8d23477feea46f05f0d5405aee5f9b110d5b86d86e2e4dd" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/f44fb6925196a9ad9c5e370efad7055bfa4d3b57f6e8601730e9bc6f87e27b21" :answer/id #uuid "6e0d3cd9-78d0-5801-b268-5ffd73ca96c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/3106d29ec84ff4a540fd8dad587c31084ffb5bcb597f43d1abcf43548fc86090" :answer/id #uuid "7c73a7b2-a2bf-518a-beb1-31fbbadf0c5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6-{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/61b414f03fb19f29a438aafd2c26809ce879d88ba614d981b6366b238a05ca82" :answer/id #uuid "d70f278f-f71b-563b-90a5-a72e4490f97d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/ecdf59a6922e0a715d091f39d1edb555e71827b1cef672bec6f966d7329a486d" :answer/id #uuid "be7b681a-d4b7-5605-ba2e-22acaaed6363" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/ccfdfe1553bd07a74184fa884521de80a6a997a2cb3a9bc67957d68dfb3f0e82" :answer/id #uuid "7c9aa96a-e438-54ed-91f2-a9cd9b89c2af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{6{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4" :answer-field/id #uuid "40c6d291-cf90-51ae-b2e3-e5400146213f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/f44fb6925196a9ad9c5e370efad7055bfa4d3b57f6e8601730e9bc6f87e27b21" "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/3106d29ec84ff4a540fd8dad587c31084ffb5bcb597f43d1abcf43548fc86090" "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/61b414f03fb19f29a438aafd2c26809ce879d88ba614d981b6366b238a05ca82" "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/ecdf59a6922e0a715d091f39d1edb555e71827b1cef672bec6f966d7329a486d" "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/ccfdfe1553bd07a74184fa884521de80a6a997a2cb3a9bc67957d68dfb3f0e82"] :answer-field/correct "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4/f44fb6925196a9ad9c5e370efad7055bfa4d3b57f6e8601730e9bc6f87e27b21" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339145" :question/id #uuid "b18cb65d-b781-5075-91bf-6c656ac3ed30" :question/math-academy-id "q-339145" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y=x,\\,y(0)=5\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $Q(x)=x.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (x/6)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot y & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}) & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12})\\text{d}x & =\\int x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =\\int 6{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}+C \\\\ y & =6+C{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=5$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =6+C{e}^{-{0}^{2}/12} \\\\ 5 & =6+C \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-339145/ma-source-field/320d1be803bb92f6891699e87ddb1b7613430ee22555ea0d5185515a362d4fda" "q-339145/ma-source-field/0c2230b8c2101b9a8e7125455dc63ad6dbda35145ec292f9c45f0336c5f04ab4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01c5809f-cb10-5192-b646-13036813137d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339145"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339169/ma-source-field/140344d2b525b8885d5a355e58eca9102d84cc640cc3f9209aaa3fd93529e927/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "198c8e7f-e98a-5eaf-a800-18f9ff78792b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339169/ma-source-field/140344d2b525b8885d5a355e58eca9102d84cc640cc3f9209aaa3fd93529e927/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "299cc599-8438-5e31-a5d0-214b9d59050d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339169/ma-source-field/140344d2b525b8885d5a355e58eca9102d84cc640cc3f9209aaa3fd93529e927/1028b50c0cbb7a1b02cf8d6690d1353e6705478818994ba94f4b73db89dd35ba" :answer/id #uuid "e79a7021-331e-58f2-b8f6-85a889c84c54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339169/ma-source-field/140344d2b525b8885d5a355e58eca9102d84cc640cc3f9209aaa3fd93529e927/7a1faa903ae4