answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-339910/ma-source-field/699f2efcac589426b782437ef3ec23b6d2abadcd59aca6c272a5c5ab3fbce761/0bf1508834bc49a787d08b8b33b37a3b65ce7dcf0b50406376ecc50165a704b6" "q-339910/ma-source-field/699f2efcac589426b782437ef3ec23b6d2abadcd59aca6c272a5c5ab3fbce761/f073cec77042b855fcc95ae59e5c07a0d566930857e27de8effde7dcda1f144f"] :answer-field/correct "q-339910/ma-source-field/699f2efcac589426b782437ef3ec23b6d2abadcd59aca6c272a5c5ab3fbce761/0bf1508834bc49a787d08b8b33b37a3b65ce7dcf0b50406376ecc50165a704b6" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339910" :question/id #uuid "af1eb49f-2047-54c5-af74-dcf0eb0576e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-339910" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}=-2x\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{x}^{3}+B,$ where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)=x$ \n{{field-1}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{2}$ \n{{field-2}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$\\,\\,$\n$y(x)=$ \n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\n$\\,$\nwhere \n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." :question/worked-solution "For an inhomogeneous differential equation, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}_{c}(x)$ is the complementary solution (the general solution of the corresponding homogeneous equation), and\n\n- ${y}_{p}(x)$ is a particular solution of the original inhomogeneous equation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check which of the two given functions is a particular solution of our inhomogeneous equation:\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)=x,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =(x)^{′}=1, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(1)^{′}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(0)-2x(1)=-2x.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)=x$ $\\text{is}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{2},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{2})^{′}=2x, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(2x)^{′}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(2)-2x(2x)=-2x.\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{2}$ $\\text{isn't}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nWe are told that the complementary solution of our equation is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{x}^{3}+B.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =A{x}^{3}+B+x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A\\text{ and }B$ are arbitrary constants." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339910/ma-source-field/2e12a8031c21fc9c0a30548dd8367b45e43b43b0e9bd202ac7215eff517889ac" "q-339910/ma-source-field/73556e46bd29c2f6d8c88c7de265b90dd7acd5c3ca33cefb85a7e86ad23e1a0d" "q-339910/ma-source-field/5707babac6abacd23910c19a43d0ecdb9727a5ce4514767d62d8e4a4ccd608b7" "q-339910/ma-source-field/a92bc2e4acdaa961945b09b071651317f03d040bff790fc35dd3e64df73c9b5f" "q-339910/ma-source-field/699f2efcac589426b782437ef3ec23b6d2abadcd59aca6c272a5c5ab3fbce761"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7640be27-8277-5a9c-bf14-83bcc7a38604"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339910"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339913/ma-source-field/2e12a8031c21fc9c0a30548dd8367b45e43b43b0e9bd202ac7215eff517889ac/d029defaf49fa0f42d047edac2d8d14ec0638f11d1f3b80a99f458177dd8f219" :answer/id #uuid "89a0b1c8-9210-56e2-99b9-b8e5988b2240" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "is" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339913/ma-source-field/2e12a8031c21fc9c0a30548dd8367b45e43b43b0e9bd202ac7215eff517889ac/61af73b8e8ead9835a9b9a8e325b35ee392bbd1ef8d56b833ee0389146eb9f6a" :answer/id #uuid "2f61fa9d