wer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-340418/ma-source-field/34dd933bdc19bef7b12fc319a7e6004e2ca31bdb6da88a5b40e4afd7fc6b6b6d/983c93ff924ce5335f06428d96bd6f82a7abb1627095a23e2963f553ef0296e0" "q-340418/ma-source-field/34dd933bdc19bef7b12fc319a7e6004e2ca31bdb6da88a5b40e4afd7fc6b6b6d/9c3ad2c99c8849591338356a35cfd0ab8652729452f525ac155ad08b409d17c0" "q-340418/ma-source-field/34dd933bdc19bef7b12fc319a7e6004e2ca31bdb6da88a5b40e4afd7fc6b6b6d/f2bd9344b910498b1b4df38f1e4c05a086ad39b15271d4c6eed5d21d2e1a96bf" "q-340418/ma-source-field/34dd933bdc19bef7b12fc319a7e6004e2ca31bdb6da88a5b40e4afd7fc6b6b6d/fef211dbcd336bdcbd5594509c81611107f2303607507326fb301c385c8dec6b" "q-340418/ma-source-field/34dd933bdc19bef7b12fc319a7e6004e2ca31bdb6da88a5b40e4afd7fc6b6b6d/c9302d6fc4078e95743c391fcf29b3751e7cd09f1a7785d959c7ea339e6e612b" "q-340418/ma-source-field/34dd933bdc19bef7b12fc319a7e6004e2ca31bdb6da88a5b40e4afd7fc6b6b6d/985a3004dd75f58adf4800f79ca9f270ef6c1e2245954934e339cf8733830705"] :answer-field/correct "q-340418/ma-source-field/34dd933bdc19bef7b12fc319a7e6004e2ca31bdb6da88a5b40e4afd7fc6b6b6d/983c93ff924ce5335f06428d96bd6f82a7abb1627095a23e2963f553ef0296e0" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "aa20d8e3-c4d9-5112-bd9c-ec30f6aaa6fe"] :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{5}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{5}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{20}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{20}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-10\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & ={a}_{5}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{5} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{5} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340418/ma-source-field/d2ddc04874cf769c95258327f5f65f6d38ddf09a3120a1008dbeb3f4ed83e0f4" "q-340418/ma-source-field/7c61b514de35d69f61bccd9417235fcc29fb67f25968dcf9ee5704f3779fda99" "q-340418/ma-source-field/34dd933bdc19bef7b12fc319a7e6004e2ca31bdb6da88a5b40e4afd7fc6b6b6d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-340638/ma-source-field/e69c06b0e7200916289055202f0a7b3899930d258db4281be6b132ee7fc4fa45/88495b37fd40b97208105b443db68c41f90a179f8d88bbe2da56b16059fcc3a5" :answer/id #uuid "fef36346-1430-5b7e-8f8d-dbd4ef5452d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340638/ma-source-field/e69c06b0e7200916289055202f0a7b3899930d258db4281be6b132ee7fc4fa45/bc752a1e12a0f5b97333fedd6867fa12839ca1039ec4919f451f86f5363c162e" :answer/id #uuid "681611df-aafb-58e2-b2fd-60ed1c5a8c81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340638/ma-source-field/e69c06b0e7200916289055202f0a7b3899930d258db4281be6b132ee7fc4fa45/bd187683f018878cd5f96e362b562c9007466f0bc0a77fdb0133d33dcd14d89b" :answer/id #uuid "dca82b61-b202-5c4b-8b2a-4f67990862a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/