alidate]} {:db/id "q-340638/ma-source-field/976cebddea7d9adbd6cd3413601e8ee22b3fac0677ff52e5f30421931313f3eb/c21966a44f0256a1e84c6c88a8e6094e28390cb621205d9c41b88b14f07ebdac" :answer/id #uuid "07510649-4bdf-56eb-8d9c-ed267705e564" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340638/ma-source-field/976cebddea7d9adbd6cd3413601e8ee22b3fac0677ff52e5f30421931313f3eb/a4c88eac0996a22fbcaedae9c883bde66327083f967753c1b919258a6d391cc3" :answer/id #uuid "0e3eeb27-01e0-5659-a89f-03c69d0adcb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340638/ma-source-field/976cebddea7d9adbd6cd3413601e8ee22b3fac0677ff52e5f30421931313f3eb/1f45e19b3325533845bb26e03f5e7ef2c9d153a720b5dd70782910f600225133" :answer/id #uuid "8748773f-b48a-58ec-b951-7e2f13629f66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340638/ma-source-field/976cebddea7d9adbd6cd3413601e8ee22b3fac0677ff52e5f30421931313f3eb" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b23de8e-d2ee-5400-a7e2-b5cd4049a1e7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-340638/ma-source-field/976cebddea7d9adbd6cd3413601e8ee22b3fac0677ff52e5f30421931313f3eb/aa772e7d2fc132d53d15e08aff5961c21387632f0d92ccd2d06c06096ca257e5" "q-340638/ma-source-field/976cebddea7d9adbd6cd3413601e8ee22b3fac0677ff52e5f30421931313f3eb/caceb1c6c66806fc7ac9f8ceeac483b584fb9207d7e9a350984c325f7bcc7017" "q-340638/ma-source-field/976cebddea7d9adbd6cd3413601e8ee22b3fac0677ff52e5f30421931313f3eb/cce9f716b8f939b202dfd1e5f98504e9c482c918eef9640f7cefb463a0744fc2" "q-340638/ma-source-field/976cebddea7d9adbd6cd3413601e8ee22b3fac0677ff52e5f30421931313f3eb/c21966a44f0256a1e84c6c88a8e6094e28390cb621205d9c41b88b14f07ebdac" "q-340638/ma-source-field/976cebddea7d9adbd6cd3413601e8ee22b3fac0677ff52e5f30421931313f3eb/a4c88eac0996a22fbcaedae9c883bde66327083f967753c1b919258a6d391cc3" "q-340638/ma-source-field/976cebddea7d9adbd6cd3413601e8ee22b3fac0677ff52e5f30421931313f3eb/1f45e19b3325533845bb26e03f5e7ef2c9d153a720b5dd70782910f600225133"] :answer-field/correct "q-340638/ma-source-field/976cebddea7d9adbd6cd3413601e8ee22b3fac0677ff52e5f30421931313f3eb/aa772e7d2fc132d53d15e08aff5961c21387632f0d92ccd2d06c06096ca257e5" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340638" :question/id #uuid "df849e8a-df1b-5b2f-bbc1-5b6e2ad9aeb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-340638" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{3}+5x$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{6}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{6}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{24}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-12\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={a}_{6}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{6} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{6} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340638/ma-source-field/e69c06b0e7200916289055202f0a7b3899930d258db4281be6b132ee7fc4fa45" "q-340638/