7-a3f2-889c117ed67e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340655" :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{kt}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)=\\frac{{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}}{2}}+L{\\frac{{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{3t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-3t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,s>3 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3},\\,s>-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{3t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-3t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s+3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+3)+(s-3)}{(s-3)(s+3)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}-9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{3t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (3,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-3t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-3,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(3,\\infty )\\cap (-3,\\infty )=(3,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340655/ma-source-field/66d673b37f53c53c1822c38929b36b10d07902ef54a8424c5f3d238908b9b18b" "q-340655/ma-source-field/542fd8e56a65509b4e009aca1a7c7b50a108c81f909d8f6d6c3d3c38d72368e7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c086bc97-415d-52c9-b26a-02dc8aebef33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340655"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "dfbe5295-15de-5429-ac7d-1288d0b2be34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "2134b48b-4f80-54ce-97ca-e2ded504ec18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "4d231c1e-d79b-5508-b44e-84b13e3b138c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "deda8e08-d6bd-5e0e-ae0c-00112e17523f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea71ffc-f171-5611-bfc4-d57724eb7008" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951"] :answer-field/correct "q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669/ma-source-field/13b48389b4236cfb5db6ea01fcdefd08a2c199b9ada9c0e8fe0c460a433cbd22/61bbf40bf0728127bc167767b5af83361c3acbddac67f4a51d278c010c10af58" :answer/id #uuid "7f4020d2-476a-5794-a6f2-3d8b125330ae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669/ma-source-field/13b48389b4236cfb5db6ea01fcdefd08a2c199b9ada9c0e8fe0c460a433cbd22/45748e934ef4660a4b62ead5bf1f91dfb438725115d7289eb41fe950d2ed803d" :answer/id #uuid "8433c533-4904-5d92-885f-bbcd959dd940" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669/ma-source-field/13b48389b4236cfb5db6ea01fcdefd08a2c199b9ada9c0e8fe0c460a433cbd22" :answer-field/id #uuid "199c37d6-b74a-50da-a86e-fce04acf3561" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-340669/ma-source-field/13b48389b4236cfb5db6ea01fcdefd08a2c199b9ada9c0e8fe0c460a433cbd22/61bbf40bf0728127bc167767b5af83361c3acbddac67f4a51d278c010c10af58" "q-340669/ma-source-field/13b48389b4236cfb5db6ea01fcdefd08a2c199b9ada9c0e8fe0c460a433cbd22/45748e934ef4660a4b62ead5bf1f91dfb438725115d7289eb41fe950d2ed803d"] :answer-field/correct "q-340669/ma-source-field/13b48389b4236cfb5db6ea01fcdefd08a2c199b9ada9c0e8fe0c460a433cbd22/45748e934ef4660a4b62ead5bf1f91dfb438725115d7289eb41fe950d2ed803d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340669" :question/id #uuid "3d6ca311-b229-51f5-b6ee-b805697465fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-340669" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),1⟩=$ \n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ and $g(x)=1$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the inner product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),1⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-6\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ and $g(x)=1$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340669/ma-source-field/b614f8329a24099a8d5aab94d6a3a433e41044138426ddd504147c816f76b992" "q-340669/ma-source-field/13b48389b4236cfb5db6ea01fcdefd08a2c199b9ada9c0e8fe0c460a433cbd22"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fadf4f64-3569-56b2-98e1-f6681892054a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340669"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340806/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50/323c3707f259ac463f43078adb40da54bd6fbd62183256b458b52b49dc2a9da0" :answer/id #uuid "d6fb8e02-c2ed-54c2-a769-c0f5e618e887" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340806/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be968afd490c200de57c59561755" :answer/id #uuid "82f2576e-7f7d-514c-b7d3-b07f1e9d3631" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340806/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50" :answer-field/id #uuid "35a58589-56cd-5637-b523-03f859fac5b6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-340806/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50/323c3707f259ac463f43078adb40da54bd6fbd62183256b458b52b49dc2a9da0" "q-340806/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be968afd490c200de57c59561755"] :answer-field/correct "q-340806/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50/f19e6df58422d7fb01cce9bdb84691d7edb0be968afd490c200de57c59561755" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340806/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589/d1f6c915b4e3a1496843bec633b4d1faefcdef0d6c86e2f095279d4c052efb98" :answer/id #uuid "1b091b7e-9971-5f89-be72-b0882bfa2d62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340806/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589/ad5bfb9ccc3a6d948c3146ce91a4641b42b6fbd31026ea9a2acd2a98208ac3fa" :answer/id #uuid "34d21a9d-340e-5cb4-a005-7da885a8f606" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "sine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340806/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589" :answer-field/id #uuid "52a06cf5-506a-5aec-8bcd-ea5d4fda8897" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-340806/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589/d1f6c915b4e3a1496843bec633b4d1faefcdef0d6c86e2f095279d4c052efb98" "q-340806/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589/ad5bfb9ccc3a6d948c3146ce91a4641b42b6fbd31026ea9a2acd2a98208ac3fa"] :answer-field/correct "q-340806/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589/d1f6c915b4e3a1496843bec633b4d1faefcdef0d6c86e2f095279d4c052efb98" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340806" :question/id #uuid "8afd30f6-9418-5f9f-a8dd-bdb05d34a03e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340806" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the \n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ we have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${a}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{odd}$ and the $\\text{cosine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340806/ma-source-field/74c64641a2eb54858c89f7472cbd906d97a730a2eed168f86c785bc136849c50" "q-340806/ma-source-field/d2ea1b4f0ba852655c4c3ed6ebb9c6d8277c44c0dc8ac3ddd9dcabf3f9970589"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:d