db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340883/ma-source-field/9d68d3ee145105e7c621bfcd1e46431fc57b8f8358ad84eccd916de0fcdf86b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "3811f53b-a1af-5f49-ab19-7ecfb660367f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-340883/ma-source-field/9d68d3ee145105e7c621bfcd1e46431fc57b8f8358ad84eccd916de0fcdf86b3/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c" "q-340883/ma-source-field/9d68d3ee145105e7c621bfcd1e46431fc57b8f8358ad84eccd916de0fcdf86b3/0effe7e24c5ac375d36624eab032951c53d6e3342a23114dc3ad5c93ba6d6cf8" "q-340883/ma-source-field/9d68d3ee145105e7c621bfcd1e46431fc57b8f8358ad84eccd916de0fcdf86b3/8ec194ddd369d933f19adb1373346bc1deb09c766eb6cb64c74a6206a7328cea"] :answer-field/correct "q-340883/ma-source-field/9d68d3ee145105e7c621bfcd1e46431fc57b8f8358ad84eccd916de0fcdf86b3/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340883" :question/id #uuid "94c1a445-854c-59cd-8bb7-f1e99e5361c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-340883" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ for $f(t)=u(t-2)+u(t-5),$ where $u$ is the unit step function.$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<0 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise functions $u(t-2)$ and $u(t-5),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t-2) & ={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<2 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 2\\end{aligned} \\\\ u(t-5) & ={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<5 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 5.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nu(t-2)+u(t-5)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<2 \\\\ 1,\\, & 2\\le t<5 \\\\ 2,\\, & t\\ge 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}0\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{5}1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the second integral diverges for $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{5}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s}]}_{2}^{5}+2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{5}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-sa}-{e}^{-5s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}(0-{e}^{-5s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-5s}}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s},\\,s>0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-340883/ma-source-field/fc46d5b6de75245b32ca5323c5a36bebf85fd53f85f734830bbfc95ac99c37ad" "q-340883/ma-source-field/9d68d3ee145105e7c621bfcd1e46431fc57b8f8358ad84eccd916de0fcdf86b3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ec39e02-0c39-5aa4-90e2-3477259d6262"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340883"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186222031 :question/answer-fields 17592186220824] {:db/id "q-341129/ma-source-field/ac691fe3a052c91fc5497bf03df7e2fd1487aec1ca8380fe97adf29d62d60a9e/ef8a69cb660449e64835b31d26955ef0433e1eb49332071bb2f143d8ceea26