4e85dabb5082358af9360d93c7ce717fcea0db3670310b8eab46db4fc35b5" "q-341140/ma-source-field/a0fa937a4c48535f455a5dbb0b253157c2a593693e796d1d130ddfe88ad5a7e3/46af63e5816bfe37d9562c002d5969dd8f5406eadefe6e67411268361eaf7936"] :answer-field/correct "q-341140/ma-source-field/a0fa937a4c48535f455a5dbb0b253157c2a593693e796d1d130ddfe88ad5a7e3/6d8328509dacdbd6081a140366edb8e7c70691a106f66361e38a49ffe1445dee" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341140" :question/id #uuid "f89dc302-60ce-5bd9-b567-660590ce563f" :question/math-academy-id "q-341140" :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{kt}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)=\\frac{{e}^{8t}-{e}^{-8t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{8t}-{e}^{-8t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{8t}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{-8t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{8t}}{2}}-L{\\frac{{e}^{-8t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{8t}}-\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-8t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{8t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-8},\\,s>8 \\\\ L{{e}^{-8t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+8},\\,s>-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{8t}}-\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-8t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-8}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-8}-\\frac{1}{s+8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+8)-(s-8)}{(s-8)(s+8)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{16}{{s}^{2}-64}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{s}^{2}-64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{8t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (8,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-8t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-8,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(8,\\infty )\\cap (-8,\\infty )=(8,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341140/ma-source-field/91fbb6d4c2394c753bfa4cffcf19ac3da379634884f86b8f52164798a88ebdc9" "q-341140/ma-source-field/a0fa937a4c48535f455a5dbb0b253157c2a593693e796d1d130ddfe88ad5a7e3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c086bc97-415d-52c9-b26a-02dc8aebef33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341140"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308/ma-source-field/e30afc2e7313b898feb4460df4af6ac33b78f8db6bef3d136429e4401b2e5812/808fa46739c1202a0150843e269951816b496dece9704c17e07f1f61b9a5f26f" :answer/id #uuid "fd0b285c-99a5-5dc6-b53e-349ca170a4bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308/ma-source-field/e30afc2e7313b898feb4460df4af6ac33b78f8db6bef3d136429e4401b2e5812/f7403f6eb802785afdec6495efd96521e1f3f038e252c23af16c3565311efdc0" :answer/id #uuid "330f62f3-2b9c-5888-9cec-d52701d82d24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨1,1⟩}{⟨f(x),1⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308/ma-source-field/e30afc2e7313b898feb4460df4af6ac33b78f8db6bef3d136429e4401b2e5812/3f4ac37971f00eead06694aa71f9cbcfaf9065005c7cf75ed97a13a90356ff24" :answer/id #uuid "e3d09424-4779-58cb-a9a8-a20b503a58f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308/ma-source-field/e30afc2e7313b898feb4460df4af6ac33b78f8db6bef3d136429e4401b2e5812/01ead8253f26db744369c0ee0a10ccde3064b560f7d8dbf95f0e2151f8586fd1" :answe