th :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308/ma-source-field/5d60bd6d186d6bca6bfa36ca719e46d67e1e05e0eb1d09ae5b460342e3a5e599/67554054b12d5aba305b18db51e56ab64e5990c3dbb57596462cb1db6c6e380f" :answer/id #uuid "14f752d4-26f3-5b55-951a-267514a31272" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308/ma-source-field/5d60bd6d186d6bca6bfa36ca719e46d67e1e05e0eb1d09ae5b460342e3a5e599" :answer-field/id #uuid "40e8826c-c720-5c71-8e60-9efc9028ee9f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-341308/ma-source-field/5d60bd6d186d6bca6bfa36ca719e46d67e1e05e0eb1d09ae5b460342e3a5e599/85f419139c3932e1f4939f3dda2f61e0be06a7afe61eaf1d863582a15ba53de4" "q-341308/ma-source-field/5d60bd6d186d6bca6bfa36ca719e46d67e1e05e0eb1d09ae5b460342e3a5e599/dc9cafd927906d4e6d622eca6b2d98f3e54440fda6f53f8615fa398e6253aa9a" "q-341308/ma-source-field/5d60bd6d186d6bca6bfa36ca719e46d67e1e05e0eb1d09ae5b460342e3a5e599/cc6744f8d99f3b1f7e72cc930221acf54df3d62bd21b63e469b40b1a86f013bb" "q-341308/ma-source-field/5d60bd6d186d6bca6bfa36ca719e46d67e1e05e0eb1d09ae5b460342e3a5e599/00cf2981dc86733a603826a01923a100ca9761048843c165757d3bb8a288c81e" "q-341308/ma-source-field/5d60bd6d186d6bca6bfa36ca719e46d67e1e05e0eb1d09ae5b460342e3a5e599/67554054b12d5aba305b18db51e56ab64e5990c3dbb57596462cb1db6c6e380f"] :answer-field/correct "q-341308/ma-source-field/5d60bd6d186d6bca6bfa36ca719e46d67e1e05e0eb1d09ae5b460342e3a5e599/dc9cafd927906d4e6d622eca6b2d98f3e54440fda6f53f8615fa398e6253aa9a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341308" :question/id #uuid "73b220ad-78ed-5227-b775-ed2065f7b0fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-341308" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=3x+1$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{0}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨1,1⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x]}_{-0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & =\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩ \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩} \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341308/ma-source-field/e30afc2e7313b898feb4460df4af6ac33b78f8db6bef3d136429e4401b2e5812" "q-341308/ma-source-field/9b3aa66ada7ccc360817678a599a2af3eade9efa16951604f85ccd4cba0a5568" "q-341308/ma-source-field/5d60bd6d186d6bca6bfa36ca719e46d67e1e05e0eb1d09ae5b460342e3a5e599"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341308"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341448/ma-source-field/be2b567a955e9b13a1dd37ef10726ee88f68b964ce253e6ad5059251b0efc807/4cb110938a7e6898ee80b6d3e5157678df8d1c1f6b204fe0d40306233404f9b4" :answer/id #uuid "b0648719-f6f1-5582-a9c7-b2e40208d75c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{3(1-s)}}{s-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341448/ma-source-field/be2b567a955e9b13a1dd37ef10726ee88f68b964ce253e6ad5059251b0efc807/71f3dd2296044b6bd586c69527b0a3ba4e84f5c46e6f23774a004c12e73773f9" :answer/id #uuid "edaa60e1-e666-514b-893d-b9aec909db8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{3(1-s)}}{s+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341448/ma-source-field/be2b567a955e9b13a1dd37ef10726ee88f68b964ce253e6ad5059251b0efc807/4fd56f45cd4748c6a8278f6973d85106fec1007c2c86717ed5146ed0becffd03" :answer/id #uuid "ce80b731-5ad8-572d-9659-a7d36ed14cbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{3(1-s)}}{s-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341448/ma-source-field/be2b567a955e9b13a1dd37ef10726ee88f68b964ce253e6ad5059251b0efc807/31c24af6dd6058becc63aced515e26db975152db3e5b7ecc4335c9b0d5d72708" :answer/i