text :answer/value "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x>0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343293/ma-source-field/51fa37a1f389389d76b0f2944eb7233c9cd95d4bf6fe8a173ea7c6a88b18c033" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ab8824e-5b62-51f7-bcc4-ce3c21af44e9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-343293/ma-source-field/51fa37a1f389389d76b0f2944eb7233c9cd95d4bf6fe8a173ea7c6a88b18c033/def9e284c04ff88f4501b741fdfd679144aa2f6e42b9c1ec7d4a2217819cc46c" "q-343293/ma-source-field/51fa37a1f389389d76b0f2944eb7233c9cd95d4bf6fe8a173ea7c6a88b18c033/4ddf0edc896c1f1ae6c38e2226560fa57e92098045c3c07394f525b12ebbd5f4" "q-343293/ma-source-field/51fa37a1f389389d76b0f2944eb7233c9cd95d4bf6fe8a173ea7c6a88b18c033/a8a92ea07ac7485e9fd6d2e4cc37ff1cfe2285f70b07eaedfdf36fc578c9e108"] :answer-field/correct "q-343293/ma-source-field/51fa37a1f389389d76b0f2944eb7233c9cd95d4bf6fe8a173ea7c6a88b18c033/def9e284c04ff88f4501b741fdfd679144aa2f6e42b9c1ec7d4a2217819cc46c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343293" :question/id #uuid "4acb3708-3f85-57a1-975e-b6f23d95dbae" :question/math-academy-id "q-343293" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions to the second-order homogeneous differential equation above, where $Q(x)$ is continuous on $(0,\\infty ).$ The Wronskian satisfies $W(2)=0.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\nThe Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies the following first-order differential equation:\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)={{field-1}}W(x)\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get\n\n$$\nW={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, using the fact that $W(2)=0,$ we obtain \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=2x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-2xW(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-2xW \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-2x\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-{x}^{2}+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{-{x}^{2}} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(2)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(2) & =C{e}^{-{2}^{2}} \\\\ 0 & =C{e}^{-4} \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $W(x)=0\\text{ for all }x>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343293/ma-source-field/9a6eda78eaa1b9eafbc915f8c884e2aad6c096029893f39a4ad60d52779e0983" "q-343293/ma-source-field/2584f06a97433b6c870ec7fed0dbc29026b46168e9c805c13e2067b6746e256c" "q-343293/ma-source-field/51fa37a1f389389d76b0f2944eb7233c9cd95d4bf6fe8a173ea7c6a88b18c033"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "734fe467-57d6-5b3f-a61e-1e2e4624b5fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343293"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343295/ma-source-field/408f0e320c438ae74a526f6e06ea30538b74b1854956a0b11a09ee58df5e2f4b/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "6418d95c-2071-5910-935c-316e5a6e14e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343295/ma-source-field/408f0e320c438ae74a526f6e06ea30538b74b1854956a0b11a09ee58df5e2f4b/18318f85a88deafb973a2f7e4185df4f7fbf65900f8806280ad8703c50dc6174" :answer/id #uuid "a9ce1615-d523-520a-92c9-77d8376540ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3Q(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343295/ma-source-field/408f0e320c438ae74a526f6e06ea30538b74b1854956a0b11a09ee58df5e2f4b/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "7849e7e8-dd36-565f-b3df-32eaf5d73858"