28ab2645c75649fba9df4af5d/fe89c465453197437cdcdcc0882c95d7b7a7ea57f589da4309555f3cec88e00a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343855" :question/id #uuid "15f5a0b9-1297-5188-a047-103209518fed" :question/math-academy-id "q-343855" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}-3y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}} & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,-3(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,\\,=-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -3\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{a}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{b}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,=-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the coefficients next to sines and cosines, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{a}_{n}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{b}_{n}=\\frac{6}{n\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=\\frac{4}{3},$ which means the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nNext, from the second equation, ${b}_{n}=\\frac{9{a}_{n}}{n\\pi }.$ Substituting this into the third equation, gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3(\\frac{9{a}_{n}}{n\\pi })=\\frac{6}{n\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=-\\frac{18}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{9{a}_{n}}{n\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{n\\pi }\\cdot (-\\frac{18}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{162}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼\\frac{2}{3} & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{18}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{162}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343855/ma-source-field/39f36ac048480f4dd9611e323f9ed1c335ffc5c33e572792737e7a563c025cde" "q-343855/ma-source-field/3168b2f32c894c528dbc7d931aee94fb6cd9df1d01432375671d09c3a80d3f39" "q-343855/ma-source-field/28f6b7b859983579990d4eb027b5c46aca81fa328ab2645c75649fba9df4af5d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4733fab7-18ca-5336-9aba-53212ddbf87b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343855"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343860/ma-source-field/1a0104e977313a7f0d29475904b9018aba589464008f836629d0434943d087be/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "20b43c86-9df5-5ea5-b8db-701f1d2fcb5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343860/ma-source-field/1a0104e977313a7f0d29475904b9018aba589464008f836629d0434943d087be/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "f8b221ad-c466-515a-9758-208b0b79820b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343860/ma-source-field/1a0104e977313a7f0d29475904b9018aba589464008f836629d0434943d087be/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "abc5583a-c2d4-5270-9535-e8dc76611c8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343860/ma-source-field/1a0104e977313a7f0d29475904b9018aba589464008f836629d0434943d087be/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "f5beaf63-a24e-5096-a60c-b0469d5c3b91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343860/ma-source-field/1a0104e977313a7f0d29475904b9018aba589464008f836629d0434943d087be" :answer-field/id #uuid "dfa212b9-4a9e-5ed1-977d-8a0f92f187bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-343860/ma-source-field/1a0104e