75e4ed402cec424eec14da59218a1de9d832dffe9" :answer/id #uuid "96ad6016-80ff-5081-b817-514fd1499c89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{108\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343891/ma-source-field/8ffad078a7011ff09365568afdfac2e1b769938b8a5bcc1a9e0370fc3f3db7c9/e0b79c45c7691a1c3f967e8d88372f95c1caf34fc55572a11a1592f63c85956d" :answer/id #uuid "0e910e33-e3b2-5731-a6d5-5a16e1e9ad14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{216\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343891/ma-source-field/8ffad078a7011ff09365568afdfac2e1b769938b8a5bcc1a9e0370fc3f3db7c9/24585394527cf1cd535d9aab32ec650f79307fb121548856301a5f203b818ee7" :answer/id #uuid "bc221971-12de-52c7-8478-0068ddd7a170" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{54\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343891/ma-source-field/8ffad078a7011ff09365568afdfac2e1b769938b8a5bcc1a9e0370fc3f3db7c9" :answer-field/id #uuid "9fa9bba7-0c1d-559d-9dd6-0cd8ed6cec73" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-343891/ma-source-field/8ffad078a7011ff09365568afdfac2e1b769938b8a5bcc1a9e0370fc3f3db7c9/64db6dc663cf8ff3abff2cbbda5f4ad9fceed9e7c7be79bddf21aa487895167a" "q-343891/ma-source-field/8ffad078a7011ff09365568afdfac2e1b769938b8a5bcc1a9e0370fc3f3db7c9/87b0dac8479590d15e6939175e4ed402cec424eec14da59218a1de9d832dffe9" "q-343891/ma-source-field/8ffad078a7011ff09365568afdfac2e1b769938b8a5bcc1a9e0370fc3f3db7c9/e0b79c45c7691a1c3f967e8d88372f95c1caf34fc55572a11a1592f63c85956d" "q-343891/ma-source-field/8ffad078a7011ff09365568afdfac2e1b769938b8a5bcc1a9e0370fc3f3db7c9/24585394527cf1cd535d9aab32ec650f79307fb121548856301a5f203b818ee7"] :answer-field/correct "q-343891/ma-source-field/8ffad078a7011ff09365568afdfac2e1b769938b8a5bcc1a9e0370fc3f3db7c9/87b0dac8479590d15e6939175e4ed402cec424eec14da59218a1de9d832dffe9" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343891" :question/id #uuid "d694cb78-fd17-5d72-bd5e-fb91875a20a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-343891" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}+36{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x),$ where the $1$-periodic forcing function is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below regarding the resonant component of a particular solution of the equation.\n\nThe natural frequency of the system matches the frequency of the {{field-1}} harmonic of the forcing function. \n\nConsequently, the particular solution contains a resonant term of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}={{field-2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+36{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{36{\\pi }^{2}}=6\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $1$-periodic function $(L=\\frac{1}{2})$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{(\\frac{1}{2})}=2n\\pi .\n$$\n\nFor $n=3$, we have ${\\omega }_{3}=6\\pi .$ Since ${\\omega }_{3}=\\omega ,$ the $n=3$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=3$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{3}(x)=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi x).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi x)).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{3}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi x))+x(-6\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi x)+6\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi x)) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{3}}^{″} & =-12\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi x)+12\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi x)-36{\\pi }^{2}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{3}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{3}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+36{\\pi }^{2}y=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi x):$\n\n$$\n[-12\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi x)+12\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi x)-36{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{3}}]+36{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{3}}=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi x)\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-12\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi x)+12\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi x)=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-12\\pi A=0 \\\\ 12\\pi B=\\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}A=0 \\\\ B=\\frac{1}{108\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}=\\frac{x}{108\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343891/ma-source-field/87ff251901824b571e74be979256f8762bf3f6034d13923953296424234dcad1" "q-343891/ma-source-field/8ffad078a7011ff09365568afdfac2e1b769938b8a5bcc1a9e0370fc3f3db7c9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e42e65b-6e26-5a3f-9275-25a291e13138"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343899/ma-source-field/89ee5f60d4dfc3959954021d822f140f04ba991aa514e34723f353bbecb04e67/3c8a9a23aecb09df521e3b52e6d760c65735e1de8d88cfa6550de6cd09a255ae" :answer/id #uuid "e3cd2371-beae-59d9-8d7e-94aae5b22c28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343899/ma-source-field/89ee5f60d4dfc3959954021d822f140f04ba991aa514e34723f353bbecb04e67/7ac56aea5a96727421baaac9ed3756be68edc3d274a739832f17f1a959d14e73" :answer/id #uuid "964c305f-0261-5625-959d-d4db38c740ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343899/ma-source-field/89ee5f60d4dfc3959954021d822f140f04ba991aa514e34723f353bb