2765b5fdbf115e3e3cf3f8d14fe85261e5c2b49295d1a6a8ce18256bae7773f/2afa78adbb80c716c26f0a658db0a63f4159b3e0dd4462e2365080d6c05a1fc0" :answer/id #uuid "a1876296-7211-55be-aba4-bfdcc1a01df6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{16\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343899/ma-source-field/22765b5fdbf115e3e3cf3f8d14fe85261e5c2b49295d1a6a8ce18256bae7773f/521aa58189e6d6e8f7c70e659c655275714a94dc6a961f5a01df748ef8cdea29" :answer/id #uuid "09aff7b4-dbdd-58ab-8229-b25ef4b4ba18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343899/ma-source-field/22765b5fdbf115e3e3cf3f8d14fe85261e5c2b49295d1a6a8ce18256bae7773f/74ffca6ab5a377694f466354433b47202dfd05610c16af33640f2ca61dd62d5c" :answer/id #uuid "fe23c02e-5cbf-556d-b7f3-55b796e71bfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{8\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343899/ma-source-field/22765b5fdbf115e3e3cf3f8d14fe85261e5c2b49295d1a6a8ce18256bae7773f" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef63660a-274c-5dd7-9740-8afb5e0d6094" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/choices ["q-343899/ma-source-field/22765b5fdbf115e3e3cf3f8d14fe85261e5c2b49295d1a6a8ce18256bae7773f/0d1e464c72b80a340d6a04d0bb6c63bcf7350db8bb95c08236ddc4596e9d57da" "q-343899/ma-source-field/22765b5fdbf115e3e3cf3f8d14fe85261e5c2b49295d1a6a8ce18256bae7773f/2afa78adbb80c716c26f0a658db0a63f4159b3e0dd4462e2365080d6c05a1fc0" "q-343899/ma-source-field/22765b5fdbf115e3e3cf3f8d14fe85261e5c2b49295d1a6a8ce18256bae7773f/521aa58189e6d6e8f7c70e659c655275714a94dc6a961f5a01df748ef8cdea29" "q-343899/ma-source-field/22765b5fdbf115e3e3cf3f8d14fe85261e5c2b49295d1a6a8ce18256bae7773f/74ffca6ab5a377694f466354433b47202dfd05610c16af33640f2ca61dd62d5c"] :answer-field/correct "q-343899/ma-source-field/22765b5fdbf115e3e3cf3f8d14fe85261e5c2b49295d1a6a8ce18256bae7773f/74ffca6ab5a377694f466354433b47202dfd05610c16af33640f2ca61dd62d5c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343899" :question/id #uuid "dd94ef93-5daf-566f-92be-7aef938749ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-343899" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x),$ where the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼5+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below regarding the resonant component of a particular solution of the equation.\n\nThe natural frequency of the system matches the frequency of the {{field-1}} harmonic of the forcing function. \n\nConsequently, the particular solution contains a resonant term of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}={{field-2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}}=\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $4$-periodic function $(L=2)$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nFor $n=2$, we have ${\\omega }_{2}=\\pi .$ Since ${\\omega }_{2}=\\omega ,$ the $n=2$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=2$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{2}(x)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{2}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))+x(-\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{2}}^{″} & =-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)-{\\pi }^{2}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{2}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{2}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x):$\n\n$$\n[-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)-{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{2}}]+{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2\\pi A=0 \\\\ 2\\pi B=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}A=0 \\\\ B=\\frac{1}{8\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}=\\frac{x}{8\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-343899/ma-source-field/89ee5f60d4dfc3959954021d822f140f04ba991aa514e34723f353bbecb04e67" "q-343899/ma-source-field/22765b5fdbf115e3e3cf3f8d14fe85261e5c2b49295d1a6a8ce18256bae7773f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e42e65b-6e26-5a3f-9275-25a291e13138"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343899"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343910/ma-source-field/87ff251901824b571e74be979256f8762bf3f6034d13923953296424234dcad1/3c8a9a23aecb09df521e3b52e6d760c65735e1de8d88cfa6550de6cd09a255ae" :answer/id #uuid "4123d653-3eb6-56f8-9a54-2ef04840a633" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343910/ma-source-field/87ff251901824b571e74be979256f8762bf3f6034d13923953296424234dcad1/7ac56aea5a96727421baaac9ed3756be68edc3d274a739832f17f1a959d14e73" :answer/id #uuid "5c2e6e0a-4098-5507-86d3-f9eae8b3dec8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343910/ma-source-field/87ff251901824b571e74be979256f8762bf3f6034d139